Z4 fast path),\n  3..9 (HC hashChain), 10..12 (HC optimal path), >12 clamped.\n  Note the C picks LZ4 vs LZ4HC based on `level < LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN`. BOTH must be covered.\n- `autoFlush`: 0 vs 1\n- `favorDecSpeed`: 0 vs 1\n- `stableSrc` in LZ4F_compressOptions_t: 0 vs 1\n- `stableDst` in LZ4F_decompressOptions_t: 0 vs 1\n- `skipChecksums` in LZ4F_decompressOptions_t: 0 vs 1\n\n**The FULL set of public entry points — include the LOW-LEVEL ones, not just the\none-shot `LZ4F_compressFrame`:**\n  LZ4F_compressFrame, LZ4F_compressFrameBound, LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict,\n  LZ4F_createCompressionContext, LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced,\n  LZ4F_freeCompressionContext, LZ4F_compressBegin, LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict,\n  LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict, LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce,\n  LZ4F_compressBegin_internal, LZ4F_compressBound, LZ4F_compressUpdate,\n  LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate, LZ4F_flush, LZ4F_compressEnd,\n  LZ4F_createCDict, LZ4F_createCDict_advanced, LZ4F_freeCDict,\n  LZ4F_createDecompressionContext, LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced,\n  LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext, LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext,\n  LZ4F_headerSize, LZ4F_getFrameInfo, LZ4F_decompress, LZ4F_decompress_usingDict,\n  LZ4F_getBlockSize, LZ4F_getVersion, LZ4F_isError, LZ4F_getErrorName,\n  LZ4F_getErrorCode, LZ4F_compressionLevel_max,\n  LZ4F_writeOpen, LZ4F_write, LZ4F_writeClose, LZ4F_readOpen, LZ4F_read, LZ4F_readClose\n\n**Input SHAPES / call-pattern axes the code special-cases:**\n- srcSize: 0, 1, a few bytes, exactly blockSize, blockSize-1, blockSize+1,\n  several whole blocks, many blocks, sizes far larger than blockSize\n- compressible (long runs) vs incompressible (random) data — the latter forces the\n  \"uncompressed/stored block\" path where the block header high bit is set\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` called with many SMALL chunks so that data is buffered in\n  `tmpBuff` (the tmpIn/tmpInSize buffering path), vs one big chunk, vs chunk sizes\n  that exactly hit the block boundary\n- interleaving `LZ4F_flush` between updates, with and without autoFlush\n- `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` (uncompressed blocks) — only valid with blockIndependent —\n  and mixing it with LZ4F_compressUpdate so buffered compressed data is flushed first\n- decode side: feeding the compressed frame to `LZ4F_decompress` in ONE call, and\n  byte-by-byte / small fixed-size chunks (this drives the dStage state machine through\n  every state: storeFrameHeader, getBlockHeader, storeBlockHeader, copyDirect,\n  getCBlockSize, getBlock, storeCBlock, decodeCBlock, decodeCBlock_intoTmp,\n  flushOut, getSuffix, storeSuffix, getSFrameSize, storeSFrameSize, skipSkippable)\n- decode with a dstBuffer SMALLER than the block size (forces the tmpOut path and\n  partial flushOut), vs a dst large enough\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` called BEFORE any decompress, and called mid-stream\n- `LZ4F_headerSize` on headers of every option combination (the header length varies\n  with contentSize/dictID presence)\n- dictionary axes: LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict / LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict with\n  a CDict, LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict, LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce, and decoding\n  those with LZ4F_decompress_usingDict; dict sizes 0 / small / <64KB / >64KB\n- skippable frames: decoding a skippable frame, and a skippable frame followed by a real frame\n- lz4file.c: LZ4F_writeOpen/write/writeClose then LZ4F_readOpen/read/readClose round\n  trip through a real temp FILE*, with varying read chunk sizes (1 byte, small, larger\n  than the block), varying preferences, and multi-block content\n\nWrite ONE ROW per meaningful combination, as a GitHub markdown table with EXACTLY\nthese columns:\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n\n(the last column is a literal empty checkbox `[ ]`)\n\nRules:\n- `entry point(s)` = exact public C symbol name(s) exercised by that row.\n- `configuration` = precise and TESTABLE: state every preference field value AND the\n  input shape (sizes in bytes, data character, chunk sizes, number of blocks, dict\n  size...). Be concrete enough that a test author can implement the row without\n  re-reading the C source.\n- Prune to combinations the code ACTUALLY distinguishes, but do NOT restrict to the\n  one-shot API and do NOT guess which configs \"matter\" — cover every blockSizeID,\n  both blockModes, both checksum flags, both frameTypes, contentSize present/absent,\n  dictID present/absent, the LZ4-fast AND both LZ4HC compression-level regimes,\n  autoFlush both ways, and the full entry-point list above. EVERY public symbol from\n  the list must appear in at least one row.\n- Number rows sequentially starting at 1.\n\nExpect on the order of 80-120 rows. Group with `## lz4frame.c — compression`,\n`## lz4frame.c — decompression`, `## lz4frame.c — dictionary / CDict`,\n`## lz4file.c` headings, each with its own table, but with GLOBALLY sequential row numbers.\n\nOUTPUT: write to the file:\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/CONFIGS_part2.md\n\nThen report back: total rows written, rows per section, and confirm that every public\nsymbol in the lists above appears in at least one row (list any that do not)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4346,"cache_read_input_tokens":46250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4346,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"ed6fedb5-6f46-4953-a5f6-ed33ba38b394","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:05:52.877Z"}
