ble)\n- decode with a dstBuffer SMALLER than the block size (forces the tmpOut path and\n  partial flushOut), vs a dst large enough\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` called BEFORE any decompress, and called mid-stream\n- `LZ4F_headerSize` on headers of every option combination (the header length varies\n  with contentSize/dictID presence)\n- dictionary axes: LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict / LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict with\n  a CDict, LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict, LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce, and decoding\n  those with LZ4F_decompress_usingDict; dict sizes 0 / small / <64KB / >64KB\n- skippable frames: decoding a skippable frame, and a skippable frame followed by a real frame\n- lz4file.c: LZ4F_writeOpen/write/writeClose then LZ4F_readOpen/read/readClose round\n  trip through a real temp FILE*, with varying read chunk sizes (1 byte, small, larger\n  than the block), varying preferences, and multi-block content\n\nWrite ONE ROW per meaningful combination, as a GitHub markdown table with EXACTLY\nthese columns:\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n\n(the last column is a literal empty checkbox `[ ]`)\n\nRules:\n- `entry point(s)` = exact public C symbol name(s) exercised by that row.\n- `configuration` = precise and TESTABLE: state every preference field value AND the\n  input shape (sizes in bytes, data character, chunk sizes, number of blocks, dict\n  size...). Be concrete enough that a test author can implement the row without\n  re-reading the C source.\n- Prune to combinations the code ACTUALLY distinguishes, but do NOT restrict to the\n  one-shot API and do NOT guess which configs \"matter\" — cover every blockSizeID,\n  both blockModes, both checksum flags, both frameTypes, contentSize present/absent,\n  dictID present/absent, the LZ4-fast AND both LZ4HC compression-level regimes,\n  autoFlush both ways, and the full entry-point list above. EVERY public symbol from\n  the list must appear in at least one row.\n- Number rows sequentially starting at 1.\n\nExpect on the order of 80-120 rows. Group with `## lz4frame.c — compression`,\n`## lz4frame.c — decompression`, `## lz4frame.c — dictionary / CDict`,\n`## lz4file.c` headings, each with its own table, but with GLOBALLY sequential row numbers.\n\nOUTPUT: write to the file:\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/CONFIGS_part2.md\n\nThen report back: total rows written, rows per section, and confirm that every public\nsymbol in the lists above appears in at least one row (list any that do not).","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ieCE1Y-translated-rust/5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b/tasks/a0b529ae5a3ae9670.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
