{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jxssz23jql2ivt4o2xeanvx3mqjs3vdvqqt5vqbbwue5hrmavzxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HhghTocUcLcToJsT8dsA6c","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Write xxhash differential tests","prompt":"Write Rust differential integration tests for the xxhash portion of an LZ4 C-to-Rust translation.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\n## Context\n\n- `c_src/src/xxhash.c` + `c_src/include/xxhash.h` are the C ground truth. The C is\n  compiled with `-DXXH_NAMESPACE=LZ4_`, so ALL exported symbols are prefixed `LZ4_`:\n  `LZ4_XXH32`, `LZ4_XXH64`, `LZ4_XXH32_createState`, `LZ4_XXH32_freeState`,\n  `LZ4_XXH32_reset`, `LZ4_XXH32_update`, `LZ4_XXH32_digest`, `LZ4_XXH32_copyState`,\n  `LZ4_XXH32_canonicalFromHash`, `LZ4_XXH32_hashFromCanonical`, and the XXH64\n  equivalents, plus `LZ4_XXH_versionNumber`.\n- `src/xxhash.rs` is the Rust translation. The C code is ALWAYS correct; if outputs\n  diverge, FIX THE RUST, never the C. DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`.\n- Both are already built as shared libraries:\n  - C:    `c_src/build/liblz4.so`\n  - Rust: `target/release/liblz4.so`\n\n## MANDATORY: use the existing harness\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs` already exists and is proven working. READ IT FIRST. It provides:\n- `libs()` -> `&'static Pair` with `.c` and `.rust` fields\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol_name\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way you may obtain\n  functions. NEVER call Rust functions directly / never `use lz4::...`. Every call must\n  go through the `.so` export tables via libloading so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are\n  tested too.\n- `Rng::new(seed)` — deterministic xoshiro256** PRNG with `next_u64`, `next_u32`,\n  `byte`, `below(n)`, `range(lo,hi)`, `bool()`\n- `gen_shape(&mut rng, shape, len)`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name(shape)`, and the individual\n  generators `gen_random`, `gen_constant`, `gen_periodic`, `gen_text`, `gen_mixed`,\n  `gen_selfref`\n- `AlignedBuf::new(len, align)` and `AlignedBuf::with_offset(len, align, offset)` for\n  producing deliberately MISALIGNED pointers\n- `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c_bytes, rust_bytes)` — precise diff on mismatch\n- `XXH_OK` (0), `XXH_ERROR` (1), `XXH32_canonical_t`, `XXH64_canonical_t`\n- IMPORTANT HARNESS RULE: when comparing output buffers, pre-fill the C buffer and the\n  Rust buffer with the SAME sentinel byte (e.g. `0xAA`), then compare the FULL buffer.\n  Using different fills produces false positives on untouched bytes.\n\nStart your file with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\n\n## What to test — read xxhash.c and cover ALL of these axes\n\n**One-shot:**\n- `LZ4_XXH32(input, len, seed)` and `LZ4_XXH64(input, len, seed)`\n- lengths: 0,1,2,3,4,5,7,8,9,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,65,127,128,129,255,256,\n  1023,1024,1025,4096,65535,65536,100000 — plus randomized lengths\n- seeds: 0, 1, 0xFFFFFFFF (XXH32) / large u64 values (XXH64), plus randomized seeds\n- all `N_SHAPES` data shapes\n- ALIGNMENT: run each length at pointer offsets 0..8 using `AlignedBuf::with_offset`,\n  because xxhash.c has distinct aligned vs unaligned read paths\n\n**Streaming state API:**\n- `LZ4_XXH32_createState` / `LZ4_XXH32_freeState` (and 64) — assert both return\n  non-NULL / same free result\n- `LZ4_XXH32_reset(state, seed)` / `LZ4_XXH64_reset(state, seed)` — compare returned\n  `XXH_errorcode`\n- `LZ4_XXH32_update(state, buf, len)` — drive the internal buffering logic by splitting\n  one input into MANY different chunk patterns:\n  - one single update of the whole input\n  - byte-at-a-time updates\n  - fixed chunk sizes 1,2,3,5,7,8,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,65\n  - RANDOM chunk sizes (seeded)\n  - chunk splits that land exactly on the internal buffer boundary (16 bytes for\n    XXH32, 32 bytes for XXH64) and one byte either side of it\n  - zero-length updates interleaved between real updates (with both NULL and non-NULL\n    pointer for the zero-length case)\n- `LZ4_XXH32_digest` / `LZ4_XXH64_digest` — must equal the one-shot hash of the same\n  total input, AND must equal between C and Rust. Also call digest MULTIPLE times in a\n  row (it must be idempotent and must agree).\n- `LZ4_XXH32_copyState` / `LZ4_XXH64_copyState` — copy mid-stream, then continue\n  updating BOTH the original and the copy with further data and compare all digests.\n  ALSO compare the raw state bytes: allocate the state with createState from each\n  library, and after each operation memcmp the state blobs. The state struct is\n  `XXH32_state_t` / `XXH64_state_t` — get their size from `xxhash.h`. If the C and Rust\n  state layouts are supposed to be identical, byte-compare them; if you find they are\n  padded differently, compare only the digests and note it in a comment.\n\n**Canonical representation:**\n- `LZ4_XXH32_canonicalFromHash(&canonical, hash)` for many hashes including 0,\n  0xFFFFFFFF, and randomized — compare the 4 canonical bytes\n- `LZ4_XXH32_hashFromCanonical(&canonical)` for all-zero, all-0xFF and randomized\n  canonical inputs — compare returned hash\n- round-trip hash -> canonical -> hash\n- same for the XXH64 pair (8 bytes)\n\n**Version:**\n- `LZ4_XXH_versionNumber()`\n\n## Error paths (Phase C) — put these in the SAME file\nGrep xxhash.c for every `XXH_ERROR` return and every NULL check, and test each:\n- `LZ4_XXH32_reset(NULL, seed)` / `LZ4_XXH64_reset(NULL, seed)`\n- `LZ4_XXH32_update(NULL, buf, len)` / `LZ4_XXH64_update(NULL, ...)`\n- `LZ4_XXH32_update(state, NULL, 0)` and `LZ4_XXH32_update(state, NULL, nonzero)` —\n  read the C carefully to see which is a defined XXH_OK vs an error; replicate whatever\n  the C actually does. If a case would segfault in C, DO NOT test it (note it in a\n  comment instead).\n- `LZ4_XXH32(NULL, 0, seed)` — check what C does for a NULL/zero-length one-shot\n- `LZ4_XXH32_digest(NULL)` if the C tolerates it; skip if it would crash\n- `LZ4_XXH32_freeState(NULL)`\n- assert C and Rust return the IDENTICAL error code, not merely \"both failed\"\n\n## Deliverable\n\nWrite ONE file: `tests/xxhash_diff.rs`.\n\nThen run it and make it PASS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test xxhash_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nUse `--release --offline`. If a test reveals a genuine divergence, FIX `src/xxhash.rs`\nto match the C exactly (and rebuild with `timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline`\nbefore re-running, since the test loads the built `.so`). Keep total runtime under\n~120 seconds; scale down iteration counts if needed but keep full axis coverage.\n\nReport back: the exact list of `#[test]` function names, the final pass/fail line, and\nany divergences you found and how you fixed them in the Rust."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2515,"cache_read_input_tokens":107353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2515,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"4db7a37e-1983-430d-96ad-99c46fc002ad","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:12:09.740Z"}
