rc > 65535` (lz4.c:1392/1431/1492) — unreachable\n  in a 64-bit build; `clearedTable` is the state a freshly zeroed / just-reset\n  context reports (lz4.c:891-906). `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` and\n  `LZ4_compress_forceExtDict` always use `byU32`.\n* `dict_directive` = `noDict | withPrefix64k | usingExtDict | usingDictCtx` (lz4.c:742).\n* `dictIssue_directive` = `noDictIssue | dictSmall` (lz4.c:743); `dictSmall` requires\n  `dictSize < 64KB && dictSize < currentOffset` (lz4.c:1747/1773/1794) or\n  `byU16 && ctx->currentOffset != 0` in `_fastReset` (lz4.c:1425/1439).\n* `limitedOutput_directive` = `notLimited | limitedOutput | fillOutput` (lz4.c:328-332).\n* `earlyEnd_directive` = `decode_full_block | partial_decode` (lz4.c:1842).\n* HC strategy = `lz4mid` (levels 1-2) | `lz4hc` hash-chain (levels 3-9) | `lz4opt`\n  optimal parser (levels 10-12) (lz4hc.c:92-116). **Three** strategies, not two.\n  `patternAnalysis` is on only when `nbSearches > 128`, i.e. level 9 in hash-chain\n  (lz4hc.c:1133); `fullUpdate` only at level >= 12 (lz4hc.c:1409).\n* `dictCtx_directive` = `noDictCtx | usingDictCtxHc` (lz4hc.c:72).\n* `HCfavor_e` = `favorCompressionRatio | favorDecompressionSpeed` (lz4hc.c:881);\n  the value is only *forwarded* to `LZ4HC_compress_optimal`, so it can only change\n  output at levels >= 10.\n\n---\n\n## lz4.c — block API\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `LZ4_compressBound`, `LZ4_sizeofState`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamState` | Pure functions, no data. Sweep `LZ4_compressBound(isize)` for isize = -1, 0, 1, 4, 5, 12, 13, 254, 255, 256, 65535, 65536, 65546, 65547, 2113929216 (`LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE`), 2113929217 (must be 0), `INT_MAX` (must be 0). `LZ4_sizeofState()` and `LZ4_sizeofStreamState()` must both equal `sizeof(LZ4_stream_t)` and equal each other. | [ ] |\n| 2 | `LZ4_versionNumber`, `LZ4_versionString` | No input. Expect exactly `11000` and the string `\"1.10.0\"` (NUL-terminated, compare bytes). | [ ] |\n| 3 | `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` | Sweep maxBlockSize = -1 (→0), 0 (clamped to 16 → 65566), 1, 15, 16, 17, 4096, 65536, 2113929216, 2113929217 (→0). | [ ] |\n| 4 | `LZ4_createStream`, `LZ4_freeStream`, `LZ4_initStream` | `LZ4_createStream()` then `LZ4_freeStream()` (non-NULL, then `LZ4_freeStream(NULL)` → 0). `LZ4_initStream(buf, sizeof(LZ4_stream_t))` on a `LZ4_stream_t`-aligned buffer → non-NULL; `size = sizeof(LZ4_stream_t)-1` → NULL; `buffer=NULL` → NULL; buffer deliberately offset by +1 byte from an aligned base → NULL. After a successful init, the first `LZ4_HASHTABLESIZE` bytes must be zero (tableType == `clearedTable`). | [ ] |\n| 5 | `LZ4_resetStream`, `LZ4_resetStreamState`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamState` | Compress a 40 KB block with `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` on a stream, then `LZ4_resetStream()` and compress the *same* block again: output must be byte-identical to a fresh stream's. Repeat with `LZ4_resetStreamState(state, NULL)` (returns 0) instead of `LZ4_resetStream`. | [ ] |\n| 6 | `LZ4_resetStream_fast`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | `LZ4_resetStream_fast` calls `LZ4_prepareTable(ctx, 0, byU32)`. Cover both prepareTable outcomes: (a) fresh stream (`tableType==clearedTable`) → no reset, `currentOffset` stays 0; (b) stream that already compressed a 100 KB block with `byU32` and has `currentOffset != 0` → table kept, `currentOffset += 64KB`. In each case compress a following 8 KB block and compare. | [ ] |\n| 7 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `srcSize = 0`, `dstCapacity = 1`. Must return 1 and write a single `0x00` token byte. Round-trip: `LZ4_decompress_safe(dst, out, 1, 0)` must return 0. Also `dstCapacity = 0` with `srcSize = 0` → 0. | [ ] |\n| 8 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Sub-`LZ4_minLength` all-literals path (`inputSize < 13` → `goto _last_literals`, lz4.c:1002): srcSize = 1, 2, 3, 4 (`MINMATCH`), 5 (`LASTLITERALS`), 11, 12 (`MFLIMIT`), each with `dstCapacity = LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)`; data = 0x41 repeated. Round-trip each. | [ ] |\n| 9 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Just-at-threshold sizes that enter the match loop: srcSize = 13 (`LZ4_minLength`), 14, 16, 17, 63, 64, 65 (`FASTLOOP_SAFE_DISTANCE` boundary in the decoder), 100. Data = incompressible pseudo-random bytes (fixed LCG seed) so every block is a single literal run. | [ ] |\n| 10 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `byU16` table type, highly compressible: srcSize = 4096, all bytes 0x00 (single match of length 4092 → `matchCode >= ML_MASK`, forces the `LZ4_write32(op,0xFFFFFFFF)` + `while (matchCode >= 4*255)` extension loop, lz4.c:1213-1223). | [ ] |\n| 11 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `byU16`, match-length extension with a *non*-multiple-of-1020 remainder: srcSize = 1039, 1040, 2059, 5000 of a single repeated byte (matchCode values 1020, 1021, 2040, ... exercise `op += matchCode/255; *op++ = matchCode%255` with remainder 0 and non-0). | [ ] |\n| 12 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `byU16`, literal-length extension: srcSize = 15, 16, 30, 269, 270, 271, 525 of incompressible pseudo-random data → last-run `lastRun >= RUN_MASK` path with 0, 1, and 2 `0xFF` continuation bytes (lz4.c:1318-1322). | [ ] |\n| 13 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `byU16`, mid-block literal run > 255: 300 random bytes, then a 64-byte repeated pattern, then the same 64-byte pattern again, then 300 random bytes. Forces `litLength >= RUN_MASK` inside the main loop (lz4.c:1123-1128) plus a match, plus a long final literal run. | [ ] |\n| 14 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `byU16` → `byU32` boundary, both sides: srcSize = 65535, 65536, 65546 (last `byU16`), 65547 (`LZ4_64Klimit`, first `byU32`), 65548, 65600. Data: 50% compressible (alternating 32-byte repeat / 32 random bytes) so the table type actually changes the emitted match set. Compare compressed bytes exactly. | [ ] |\n| 15 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `byU32`, > 64 KB: srcSize = 128 KB and 1 MB of (a) all-zero, (b) incompressible random, (c) 4 KB pattern repeated. Round-trip each; also assert compressed size < 64 KB for (a),(c). | [ ] |\n| 16 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Max-offset shape: build src = 65535 random bytes + a 32-byte marker + (65535 - 32) filler + the *same* 32-byte marker, so the only long match has offset exactly 65535 = `LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX`. Also build a variant with the marker at offset 65536 (one too far → must be rejected as \"too far\", lz4.c:1090-1093). | [ ] |\n| 17 | `LZ4_compress_fast`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `acceleration` axis with `dstCapacity = LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)` (`notLimited`), srcSize = 32 KB of 50%-compressible data. Sweep acceleration = `INT_MIN`, -1, 0 (all three → default 1), 1, 2, 3, 8, 64, 1000, 65536, 65537 (`LZ4_ACCELERATION_MAX`), 65538, `INT_MAX` (last three must produce output identical to 65537). | [ ] |\n| 18 | `LZ4_compress_fast`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Same acceleration sweep as row 17 but with srcSize = 200 KB (`byU32`) so `searchMatchNb = acceleration << LZ4_skipTrigger` skip-stepping interacts with the index-based table instead of the U16 one. | [ ] |\n| 19 | `LZ4_compress_fast`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `limitedOutput` directive: srcSize = 16 KB of incompressible random data; sweep `dstCapacity` = `LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)` (notLimited), `bound-1`, exact resulting compressed size, `size-1`, `size/2`, 17, 16, 1, 0. Every insufficient capacity must return 0 and must not write past `dstCapacity`. | [ ] |\n| 20 | `LZ4_compress_fast`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `limitedOutput` failing at the *match-length* check rather than the literal check (lz4.c:1187-1211): srcSize = 5000 all-zero, `dstCapacity` = 6, 7, 8, 10, 20 (a long match whose extension bytes do not fit). | [ ] |\n| 21 | `LZ4_compress_fast_extState`, `LZ4_sizeofState` | Caller-provided state of exactly `LZ4_sizeofState()` bytes, aligned. Cover all four internal branches: {srcSize 40000 (byU16), srcSize 100000 (byU32)} × {`dstCapacity >= LZ4_compressBound` → notLimited, `dstCapacity = bound-1` → limitedOutput}. Data = 50% compressible. Assert the state is fully re-initialised (`LZ4_initStream`) each call by running the same call twice on the same state and comparing. | [ ] |\n| 22 | `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset` | Same 4-way branch matrix as row 21 but *without* re-init, so `LZ4_prepareTable` decides. Sequence on one state: (1) `LZ4_initStream`, (2) 40000-byte byU16 block with `currentOffset == 0` → `noDictIssue`, (3) immediately a second 40000-byte byU16 block, now `currentOffset != 0` → **`dictSmall`** (lz4.c:1425-1428), (4) a 100000-byte byU32 block → tableType change forces a full table reset. Compare all four outputs. | [ ] |\n| 23 | `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset` | `LZ4_prepareTable` reset triggers, one row per trigger, each verified by comparing against a freshly-initialised state: (a) `inputSize >= 4 KB` (block of 4096 vs 4095 bytes), (b) `byU16 && currentOffset + inputSize >= 0xFFFF` (drive currentOffset to 60000 with small blocks then submit a 6000-byte block), (c) tableType change byU16→byU32, (d) fresh/cleared table (no reset at all: two consecutive 1024-byte byU16 blocks with currentOffset small). | [ ] |\n| 24 | `LZ4_compress_fast_extState`, `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset` | `byPtr` table type. Only selectable when `sizeof(void*)==4 && (uptrval)src > LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX` (lz4.c:1392). Build the library for i686 (32-bit) and compress a heap-allocated 200 KB, 1 MB buffer whose address exceeds 0xFFFF; also assert `LZ4_prepareTable`'s unconditional `tableType == byPtr` reset. On 64-bit this branch is unreachable — record that explicitly. | [ ] |\n| 25 | `LZ4_compress_destSize`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `fillOutput` directive with `targetDstSize < LZ4_compressBound(*srcSizePtr)`, `byU16`: srcSize = 40000 of 50%-compressible data; sweep targetDstSize = 1, 2, 3, 12, 13, 16, 100, 1024, 4096, 20000, and `bound-1`. Assert `*srcSizePtr` is updated to bytes consumed, `0 < ret <= targetDstSize`, and `LZ4_decompress_safe(dst, out, ret, *srcSizePtr) == *srcSizePtr`. | [ ] |\n| 26 | `LZ4_compress_destSize`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `fillOutput`, `byU32`: srcSize = 300000 (50% compressible and all-zero variants); targetDstSize = 1, 13, 500, 10000, 65536. Exercises the fillOutput match-truncation path incl. the `ip <= filledIp` hash-table clearing loop (lz4.c:1195-1207). | [ ] |\n| 27 | `LZ4_compress_destSize` | `fillOutput` degenerate: `targetDstSize >= LZ4_compressBound(*srcSizePtr)` → delegates to `LZ4_compress_fast_extState` with `notLimited`; also `*srcSizePtr = 0` with targetDstSize 1 (must return 1, `*srcSizePtr` unchanged at 0) and targetDstSize 0 (must return 0). | [ ] |\n| 28 | `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState` | Same as rows 25-27 but with an externally supplied state and explicit `acceleration` = 1, 2, 65537. Additionally assert the state is left clean (the wrapper re-runs `LZ4_initStream` on exit, lz4.c:1501): reuse the same state with `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset` afterwards and compare against a fresh state. | [ ] |\n| 29 | `LZ4_loadDict`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict` | `usingExtDict` + `noDictIssue`. Dictionary of exactly 64 KB (65536 bytes, random) in its own buffer; then compress one 8 KB block that shares 200-byte substrings with the dictionary. Assert `LZ4_loadDict` returns 65536 and the block decodes with `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`. | [ ] |\n| 30 | `LZ4_loadDict`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | `LZ4_loadDict` size branches: dictSize = 0, 1, 3, 4 (`HASH_UNIT`-1 = 7 boundary: 7 → returns 0, 8 → indexes), 7, 8, 100, 16383, 16384, 65535, 65536, 65537, 200000 (must truncate to the **last** 64 KB and return 65536). For each, follow with an 8 KB block via `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` and round-trip through `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict` with the same dict pointer/size actually retained. | [ ] |\n| 31 | `LZ4_loadDictSlow`, `LZ4_loadDict_internal`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | `_ld_slow` vs `_ld_fast` second hash-fill pass (lz4.c:1630-1643). Same dictionary (16 KB with many repeated 8-byte groups) loaded with `LZ4_loadDict` vs `LZ4_loadDictSlow`; compress the same 4 KB block after each. Outputs are expected to *differ* (slow favours the beginning of the dictionary) — capture both. Also call `LZ4_loadDict_internal` directly with `_ld_fast` and `_ld_slow` and require equality with the two wrappers. | [ ] |\n| 32 | `LZ4_loadDict`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | `usingExtDict` + **`dictSmall`** (lz4.c:1773): dictionary of 100 bytes (so `dictSize < 64 KB` and `dictSize < currentOffset` after `loadDict` bumps `currentOffset` by 64 KB), then one 2 KB block in a *separate* buffer. Repeat with dict sizes 8, 100, 4095, 4096, 16383, 16384 (dictSmall threshold discussion) and 65536 (→ `noDictIssue`). | [ ] |\n| 33 | `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`, `LZ4_saveDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` | `withPrefix64k` + `noDictIssue`: contiguous buffer, 6 sequential blocks of 16 KB each written back-to-back so `dictEnd == source` every time and prefix reaches >= 64 KB by block 5. Data has cross-block matches at distances 20 KB and 70 KB (the latter must be rejected as > `LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX`). Decode with `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` into a contiguous output buffer. | [ ] |\n| 34 | `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | `withPrefix64k` + **`dictSmall`** (lz4.c:1747-1748): `LZ4_loadDict` a 1 KB dictionary, then compress the block **immediately following the dictionary in memory** (so `dictEnd == source`) with `dictSize=1024 < 64 KB` and `dictSize < currentOffset`. Block size 2 KB, containing a match into the 1 KB prefix. | [ ] |\n| 35 | `LZ4_attach_dictionary`, `LZ4_loadDict`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | **`usingDictCtx`** (lz4.c:1770): dictStream = `LZ4_createStream` + `LZ4_loadDict(64 KB)`; workStream = fresh `LZ4_createStream` (currentOffset 0 → must be bumped to 64 KB by attach, lz4.c:1673); `LZ4_attach_dictionary(work, dict)`; then compress a **<= 4 KB** block (sizes 13, 100, 4095, 4096) that matches the dictionary. Decode with `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`. | [ ] |\n| 36 | `LZ4_attach_dictionary`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | dictCtx + `inputSize > 4 KB` → the dictCtx tables are `memcpy`'d into the working stream and the mode becomes `usingExtDict`/`noDictIssue` (lz4.c:1762-1768). Block sizes 4097, 8192, 100000. Same 64 KB dictionary as row 35; compare against row 35's `usingDictCtx` output for the overlapping content. | [ ] |\n| 37 | `LZ4_attach_dictionary` | Degenerate attach: `dictionaryStream = NULL` → `dictCtx = NULL`; dictionaryStream loaded with a 0-byte dict (`dictSize == 0`) → must **not** attach (`dictCtx` forced to NULL, lz4.c:1679-1681); attach onto a working stream whose `currentOffset` is already non-zero (must be left alone). In each case follow with a 2 KB block and compare with the no-dict result. | [ ] |\n| 38 | `LZ4_attach_dictionary`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | Second and third block after a dictCtx attach: lz4.c:991-995 sets `cctx->dictCtx = NULL` and `dictSize = inputSize` after the first block, so block 2 must silently drop the dictionary and use the previous block as prefix/extDict. Three consecutive 2 KB blocks in three *separate* buffers with a 64 KB attached dict. | [ ] |\n| 39 | `LZ4_saveDict`, `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | `LZ4_saveDict` clamping and round-trip: after compressing a 100 KB stream, call `LZ4_saveDict` with dictSize = 0, 1, 4, 1024, 65535, 65536, 65537, 200000 (must clamp to 64 KB and to the live `dict->dictSize`), into a *separate* safe buffer; then continue with one more 8 KB block and decode the whole stream with `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`. Also `safeBuffer` overlapping the source (memmove path). | [ ] |\n| 40 | `LZ4_compress_forceExtDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict` | Hidden test entry point: `notLimited`, `byU32`, `usingExtDict`, acceleration fixed at 1. Both dictIssue branches: (a) dictSize 500 (< 64 KB and < currentOffset) → `dictSmall`; (b) dictSize 65536 → `noDictIssue`. srcSize = 4 KB and 100 KB, data sharing 64-byte runs with the dictionary. Decode with `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict`. | [ ] |\n| 41 | `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | Tiny-dictionary invalidation (lz4.c:1723-1733): stream whose `dictSize` is 1, 2, or 3 (set via `LZ4_saveDict` with dictSize 1..3, or a `LZ4_loadDict` of 4..7 bytes) and `dictEnd != source`, `inputSize > 0`, `dictCtx == NULL` → dictionary must be dropped and prefix mode used. Also the `inputSize == 0` tolerance case (dictionary must be preserved). | [ ] |\n| 42 | `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` | Overlapping input/dictionary space (lz4.c:1736-1742): ring buffer of 96 KB; after several blocks, submit a block whose `source + inputSize` lands strictly inside `[dictionary, dictEnd)` so `dictSize` is recomputed and then clamped to 64 KB / zeroed if < 4. Block sizes 1 KB and 30 KB, 8 iterations wrapping the ring at least twice. | [ ] |\n| 43 | `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`, `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` | Full ring-buffer round trip: compress side uses a 96 KB input ring with `LZ4_saveDict` at wrap; decompress side uses a ring of exactly `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(maxBlockSize)` for maxBlockSize = 16, 1024, 65536. 40 blocks of pseudo-random sizes in `[1, maxBlockSize]`, mixed compressible/incompressible. Requires the decoder to take all three `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` branches (first call / rolling prefix / wrap→extDict). | [ ] |\n| 44 | `LZ4_compress_continue`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_continue` | Deprecated `_continue` wrappers: `LZ4_compress_continue` (dstCapacity implicitly `LZ4_compressBound`) and `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_continue` (explicit capacity: bound, exact, exact-1, 1). 4 sequential 8 KB blocks on a contiguous buffer after `LZ4_loadDict(32 KB)`. Output must match `LZ4_compress_fast_continue(..., acceleration=1)`. | [ ] |\n| 45 | `LZ4_compress`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput` | Deprecated one-shot wrappers. `LZ4_compress(src,dst,srcSize)` must equal `LZ4_compress_default(src,dst,srcSize,LZ4_compressBound(srcSize))`; `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput` must equal `LZ4_compress_default` for the same capacity. srcSize = 0, 1, 12, 13, 4096, 65546, 65547, 200000; capacities bound / exact / exact-1 / 0. | [ ] |\n| 46 | `LZ4_compress_withState`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_withState`, `LZ4_sizeofState` | Deprecated with-state wrappers (both hard-code acceleration 1 and call `LZ4_compress_fast_extState`). State buffer of exactly `LZ4_sizeofState()` bytes, aligned; srcSize = 0, 13, 40000 (byU16), 100000 (byU32); for `_limitedOutput_withState` also dstSize = exact and exact-1. Same state reused across calls (must be re-initialised internally each time). | [ ] |\n| 47 | `LZ4_create`, `LZ4_slideInputBuffer`, `LZ4_compress_continue`, `LZ4_freeStream` | Legacy allocation API: `LZ4_create(inputBuffer)` (argument ignored) → usable `LZ4_stream_t*`; compress 3 sequential 8 KB blocks with `LZ4_compress_continue`; `LZ4_slideInputBuffer(state)` must return `internal.dictionary` (compare against the address of the last block for prefix mode, and against the `LZ4_saveDict` buffer after a saveDict); free with `LZ4_freeStream`. | [ ] |\n| 48 | `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `decode_full_block` + `noDict`, decoder shape sweep on *valid* blocks produced by row 9-16 data. For each, call with `maxDecompressedSize` = exact original size, original+1, original+64, and original+4096 (all must succeed and return the original size). Include one block whose decoded size is < 64 = `FASTLOOP_SAFE_DISTANCE` so `safe_decode` is entered immediately (lz4.c:2076-2079), and one > 64 so the fast loop runs. | [ ] |\n| 49 | `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Match-copy offset classes in the decoder (both loops): craft/compress inputs whose matches have offset exactly 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 15, 16, 17, 64, 65535 (`LZ4_memcpy_using_offset` cases 1/2/4/default, `offset < 8` byte-wise path, `offset < 16` vs `>= 16` wildCopy32, lz4.c:2202-2206 and 2406-2418). Easiest construction: `dst = pattern[0..offset-1]` repeated to 3000 bytes, compressed with `LZ4_compress_default`. | [ ] |\n| 50 | `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Shortcut path in the safe loop (lz4.c:2230-2261) taken vs not taken: blocks with (literal length 0..14 AND match length 4..18 AND offset >= 8 AND `ip < shortiend` AND `op <= shortoend`) vs each of those five conditions individually violated. Build with a 40-byte-period pattern of 2000 bytes (shortcut hit) and a `litLength = 15` / `matchLength = 19` / `offset = 4` variant each (shortcut miss → `_copy_match`). | [ ] |\n| 51 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` | `partial_decode` + `noDict`. Reference block: 8 KB of 50%-compressible data. Sweep `(targetOutputSize, dstCapacity)` = (0,0), (0,8192), (1,1), (1,8192), (5,5), (12,12), (13,13), (63,64), (64,64), (100,100), (100,50) (dstCapacity < target → effective `MIN` = 50), (4096,4096), (4096,8192), (8191,8192), (8192,8192), (8193,8192), (8192,16384). Return value must be `min(targetOutputSize, dstCapacity, originalSize)` and the first N bytes must match the original. | [ ] |\n| 52 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` | Partial decode that must stop *inside* a literal run and *inside* a match: input = 300 random bytes + 500-byte repeat + 300 random bytes; targetOutputSize chosen to land at offsets 305, 350, 800, 1090 (mid-literal, mid-match, mid-match overlap). Exercises lz4.c:2296-2307 (literal truncation) and 2392-2404 (`MATCH_SAFEGUARD_DISTANCE` overlap copy). | [ ] |\n| 53 | `LZ4_decompress_fast`, `LZ4_uncompress` | `LZ4_decompress_unsafe_generic`, `prefixSize = 0`, no input-size knowledge. Feed only *well-formed* blocks from rows 8-16 with `originalSize` = the exact decompressed size; assert the return value equals the compressed size. Also `originalSize = 0` on the 1-byte empty block. `LZ4_uncompress` must return bit-identical results for every case (it is a pure alias). | [ ] |\n| 54 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k`, `LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k` | `withPrefix64k` directive with `lowPrefix = dest - 65536`. Contiguous 192 KB buffer: decode block 1 at offset 65536 (prefix = the 64 KB before it, produced by `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` in prefix mode). Blocks with matches at offsets 1, 100, 65535 into the prefix. `_withPrefix64k` (safe, checks srcSize) and `_fast_withPrefix64k` (`prefixSize = 65536`, unsafe) on the same block; results must be identical. | [ ] |\n| 55 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict` | `usingExtDict` with the dictionary in a *separate* buffer. Blocks from row 40. `dictSize` = 4, 100, 65535, 65536, 65537 — note `checkOffset = (dictSize < 65536)` (lz4.c:2047) so 65535 and 65536 take different code paths. Cover matches (a) entirely inside extDict, (b) straddling extDict→prefix with `restSize <= op-lowPrefix` (memcpy), (c) straddling with `restSize > op-lowPrefix` (byte-wise overlap copy, lz4.c:2187-2193). For the `_partial_` variant repeat with targetOutputSize = 1, half, exact, exact+1 and dstCapacity = target and target*2. | [ ] |\n| 56 | `LZ4_setStreamDecode`, `LZ4_createStreamDecode`, `LZ4_freeStreamDecode`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` | Explicit dictionary injection: `LZ4_createStreamDecode()`, `LZ4_setStreamDecode(sd, dict, dictSize)` for dictSize = 0 (with dictionary NULL and non-NULL), 4, 65535, 65536; then `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` on 3 blocks decoded into a buffer that is *not* adjacent to the dict (forces the `prefixEnd != dest` wrap→extDict branch on the first block after set). `LZ4_freeStreamDecode(NULL)` → 0. | [ ] |\n| 57 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` | All four internal branches, one row-item each: (a) first call, `prefixSize == 0` → `LZ4_decompress_safe`; (b) `prefixEnd == dest` and `prefixSize >= 65535` → `_withPrefix64k`; (c) `prefixEnd == dest`, `prefixSize < 65535`, `extDictSize == 0` → `_withSmallPrefix` (prefix sizes 1, 4, 100, 65534); (d) `prefixEnd == dest`, `prefixSize < 65535`, `extDictSize != 0` → `_doubleDict`; (e) `prefixEnd != dest` → `_forceExtDict`. Construct with a 96 KB ring plus one deliberate buffer switch. | [ ] |\n| 58 | `LZ4_decompress_fast_continue` | All three branches of the unsafe streaming decoder: (a) `prefixSize == 0` first call; (b) `prefixEnd == dest` continuation (`prefixSize` grows, `externalDict`/`extDictSize` carried in); (c) `prefixEnd != dest` → prefix becomes extDict → `LZ4_decompress_fast_extDict`. 10 blocks of 4 KB on a 96 KB ring with one wrap. Blocks must be exactly those produced by `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` and `originalSize` must be exact. | [ ] |\n| 59 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict` | All dispatch branches: (a) `dictSize == 0` → plain safe/unsafe; (b) `dictStart + dictSize == dest` and `dictSize >= 65535` → prefix64k; (c) contiguous and `dictSize < 65535` → smallPrefix (dictSize 1, 4, 100, 4096, 65534); (d) non-contiguous → forceExtDict / fast_extDict (dictSize 4, 100, 65536). Same block set for both entry points; `_fast_` requires exact `originalSize`. | [ ] |\n| 60 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict` | Same four dispatch branches as row 59, crossed with `(targetOutputSize, dstCapacity)` = (0, cap), (1,1), (half, half), (half, exact), (exact, exact), (exact+1, exact+1). Matches that begin in the dictionary and are truncated by the partial limit must be clamped by `length = MIN(length, oend-op)` (lz4.c:2361). | [ ] |\n| 61 | `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | Deprecated alias: for every block from rows 8-16, `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize(src, dst, isize, maxOutputSize)` must return exactly what `LZ4_decompress_safe(src, dst, isize, maxOutputSize)` returns, for maxOutputSize = exact, exact+1, exact-1 (error), 0. | [ ] |\n| 62 | `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | In-place / overlapping decompression support (`LZ4_memmove` at lz4.c:2320 and 1899): decode a block into a buffer where `dst` and `src` overlap per `LZ4_COMPRESS_INPLACE_BUFFER_SIZE` / `LZ4_DECOMPRESS_INPLACE_BUFFER_SIZE`. srcSize = 4 KB and 64 KB, compressible and incompressible. | [ ] |\n\n## lz4hc.c — HC API\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 63 | `LZ4_sizeofStateHC`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC`, `LZ4_initStreamHC` | `LZ4_sizeofStateHC()` and `LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC()` must both equal `sizeof(LZ4_streamHC_t)`. `LZ4_initStreamHC(buf, size)`: size = exact → non-NULL and `compressionLevel == 9`; size = exact-1 → NULL; buf = NULL → NULL; buf = alignedBase+1 → NULL. | [ ] |\n| 64 | `LZ4_createStreamHC`, `LZ4_freeStreamHC`, `LZ4_setCompressionLevel` | `LZ4_createStreamHC()` must come back with level = `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT` (9). `LZ4_setCompressionLevel` clamp sweep: `INT_MIN`, -1, 0 (all → 9), 1, 2, 3, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 100, `INT_MAX` (→ 12). After each set, compress the same 16 KB block with `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` and record the output; 13/100/INT_MAX must equal 12, and <=0 must equal 9. `LZ4_freeStreamHC(NULL)` → 0. | [ ] |\n| 65 | `LZ4_compress_HC`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | **`lz4mid` strategy** (levels 1 and 2 → `k_clTable[1]`/`[2]` = `{lz4mid, 2, 16}`, lz4hc.c:93-95). `compressionLevel` = 1 and 2, `dstCapacity = LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)` (`notLimited`). srcSize = 0, 1, 12, 13, 8, 9 (`LZ4MID_HASHSIZE` = 8 boundary in `LZ4MID_fillHTable`), 4096, 40000, 65547, 200000; data = all-zero, 50% compressible, incompressible. Round-trip each. | [ ] |\n| 66 | `LZ4_compress_HC`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | **`lz4hc` hash-chain strategy without patternAnalysis** (`nbSearches <= 128`, i.e. levels 3-8): compressionLevel = 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8; `notLimited`. srcSize = 13, 4096, 40000, 200000; data = 50% compressible plus one input with a 1-byte repeated run of 3000 bytes (which levels 3-8 must *not* pattern-analyse). | [ ] |\n| 67 | `LZ4_compress_HC`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | **`lz4hc` hash-chain with patternAnalysis on** (level 9, `nbSearches = 256 > 128`, lz4hc.c:1133). Level 9 (and level 0/-1/`INT_MIN`, which clamp to 9). Inputs designed to hit `LZ4HC_countPattern` / `LZ4HC_reverseCountPattern` / `LZ4HC_rotatePattern`: (a) 5000 bytes of 0xAA (1-byte pattern), (b) 5000 bytes of `AB` repeated (2-byte pattern), (c) 5000 bytes of `ABCD` repeated (4-byte pattern), (d) `ABC` repeated (3-byte, must **not** be treated as a rotatable pattern), (e) pattern run straddling a 64 KB boundary. Round-trip each. | [ ] |\n| 68 | `LZ4_compress_HC`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | **`lz4opt` optimal parser** (levels 10, 11, 12). `notLimited`. Cover the three `k_clTable` rows: 10 `{96, 64}`, 11 `{512, 128}`, 12 `{16384, LZ4_OPT_NUM=4096}` — and `fullUpdate` on only at 12 (lz4hc.c:1409). srcSize = 13, 4096, 4097 (`LZ4_OPT_NUM` boundary), 8192, 40000, 200000; data = 50% compressible, all-zero, `ABCD`-repeated. Round-trip and assert level 12 output <= level 10 output size. | [ ] |\n| 69 | `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `favorDecSpeed` axis. On a `LZ4_streamHC_t`: `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed(s, 0)` and `(s, 1)` (and `(s, 2)`, `(s, -1)` — both must behave as 1, the code stores `favor != 0`). Cross with levels 10, 11, 12 (where it is forwarded) **and** levels 2 and 9 (where it must have no effect on output). Input: 32 KB with many matches of offset < 8 and many matches of length in `(18, 36]` — both are the shapes `favorDecSpeed` changes (lz4hc.c:926-928 and 1816-1818). | [ ] |\n| 70 | `LZ4_compress_HC` | `limitedOutput` directive (`dstCapacity < LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)`, lz4hc.c:1506): srcSize = 16 KB incompressible; dstCapacity = bound-1, exact compressed size, exact-1, exact/2, 17, 1, 0 — crossed with levels 2, 3, 9, 10, 12 (all three strategies). Every insufficient capacity must return 0. | [ ] |\n| 71 | `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC`, `LZ4_sizeofStateHC` | Externally supplied state of exactly `LZ4_sizeofStateHC()` bytes. Levels 1, 2, 3, 9, 10, 12; `notLimited` and `limitedOutput`. Same state reused for several calls (each call re-runs `LZ4_initStreamHC`, so results must equal fresh-state results). Also pass a *misaligned* state (base+1) → must return 0. | [ ] |\n| 72 | `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset`, `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` | `_fastReset` skips `LZ4_initStreamHC` and relies on `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` (lz4hc.c:1504). Both `dirty` branches (lz4hc.c:1599): (a) clean state (previous call succeeded) → `dictLimit += end-prefixStart`, `prefixStart/end/dictCtx` nulled; (b) **dirty** state (force by a previous `limitedOutput` call that returned 0, which sets `ctx->dirty = 1`, lz4hc.c:1412) → full re-init. Levels 2, 9, 12. Sequence: successful 8 KB call, failing 8 KB call with dstCapacity 10, then another successful call; compare against fresh state. Also misaligned state → 0. | [ ] |\n| 73 | `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize`, `LZ4_decompress_safe` | `fillOutput` directive via `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize(state, ...)`. Levels 1, 2 (`lz4mid` fillOutput path incl. `_lz4mid_dest_overflow`, lz4hc.c:747-772), 3, 9 (`hashChain` `_dest_overflow`, lz4hc.c:1340-1361), 10, 12 (`optimal` `_dest_overflow`, lz4hc.c:2095-2117). srcSize = 40000 (50% compressible); targetDestSize = 0 (→0), 1, 2, 3, 12, 13, 20, 100, 1024, 10000. Assert `0 < ret <= targetDestSize`, `*sourceSizePtr` updated, and `LZ4_decompress_safe(dst, out, ret, *sourceSizePtr) == *sourceSizePtr`. | [ ] |\n| 74 | `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` | Contiguous streaming, prefix mode (`src == ctxPtr->end`, no `LZ4HC_setExternalDict`). `LZ4_createStreamHC` + `LZ4_setCompressionLevel(L)` for L = 2, 9, 12; 8 sequential 16 KB blocks in one 192 KB buffer with cross-block matches at 20 KB and 80 KB distance. `dstCapacity` = bound (notLimited) and bound-1 (limitedOutput). Decode with `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`. | [ ] |\n| 75 | `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | extDict mode: blocks in *separate* buffers so `src != ctxPtr->end` and `LZ4HC_setExternalDict` runs every block (lz4hc.c:1660-1678). Note `setExternalDict` calls `LZ4HC_Insert` only when `end >= prefixStart+4` and strategy != `lz4mid` — so cover levels 2 (skips Insert) and 9/12 (does Insert), and a first block of 1, 2, 3, and 4 bytes. 5 blocks of 8 KB with inter-block matches. | [ ] |\n| 76 | `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | Overlapping input/dictionary space in the HC streaming path (lz4hc.c:1706-1717), including the \"invalidate dictionary if `dictLimit - lowLimit < LZ4HC_HASHSIZE` (4)\" branch. 96 KB ring buffer, 30 blocks of pseudo-random size in `[1, 8192]`, levels 2, 9, 12. Round-trip through a matching decoder ring. | [ ] |\n| 77 | `LZ4_loadDictHC`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict` | `LZ4_loadDictHC` size and strategy branches: dictSize = 0, 1, 3, 4 (`LZ4HC_HASHSIZE`), 8, 9 (`LZ4MID_HASHSIZE`+1), 32768, 32769 (the `size > 32KB + 8` second-pass threshold in `LZ4MID_fillHTable`, lz4hc.c:506), 65536, 65537, 200000 (must truncate to the *last* 64 KB and return 65536). Crossed with level 2 (→ `LZ4MID_fillHTable`) and levels 9/12 (→ `LZ4HC_Insert(end-3)`). Follow each with one 8 KB block and round-trip via `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`. | [ ] |\n| 78 | `LZ4_loadDictHC`, `LZ4_setCompressionLevel`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | `LZ4_loadDictHC` preserves the compression level across its internal full re-init (lz4hc.c:1639-1643): set level to 1, 2, 3, 9, 10, 12 *before* `LZ4_loadDictHC(32 KB)`, then compress an 8 KB block; the level in effect must still be the one set. Compare with setting the level after loadDictHC. | [ ] |\n| 79 | `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary`, `LZ4_loadDictHC`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | **`usingDictCtxHc`** path (lz4hc.c:1463). dictStream: `LZ4_createStreamHC` + level L_d + `LZ4_loadDictHC(64 KB)`. workStream: fresh, level L_w. `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary(work, dict)` then compress a block. Cover the three `LZ4HC_compress_generic_dictCtx` branches: (a) `position >= 64 KB` → dictCtx dropped; (b) `position == 0 && srcSize > 4 KB && isStateCompatible` → dictCtx `memcpy`'d + `LZ4HC_setExternalDict` (srcSize 4097, 8192, 100000); (c) otherwise → true `usingDictCtxHc` (srcSize 13, 100, 4096). | [ ] |\n| 80 | `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | `isStateCompatible` axis (lz4hc.c:1434-1439): `mid1 ^ mid2` must be 0 for the memcpy shortcut. Cross dict level ∈ {2 (mid), 9 (hc)} with working level ∈ {2, 9, 12} and srcSize = 8192 (> 4 KB) and 1024 (<= 4 KB). The (dict=2, work=9) and (dict=9, work=2) combinations must take branch (c), not the memcpy shortcut. Also `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary(work, NULL)` → dictCtx NULL. | [ ] |\n| 81 | `LZ4HC_searchExtDict`, `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | Reach the exported `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` through `LZ4MID_searchHCDict` (lz4hc.c:410-418, selected by `select_searchDict_function` when the *dictionary* context's level is >= 3 but the working context is `lz4mid`): dict stream at level 9 or 12 with `LZ4_loadDictHC(64 KB)`, working stream at level 2, `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary`, then compress 1024 and 4096 bytes that only match inside the dictionary. Also call `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` directly with `currentBestML = MINMATCH-1`, `nbAttempts` = 0, 1, 2, 8 against a prepared dictCtx and assert `{len, off, back}`. Contrast with the `LZ4MID_searchExtDict` path (dict level 2). | [ ] |\n| 82 | `LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` | `fillOutput` in streaming mode. Levels 2, 9, 12; 4 sequential blocks of 20000 bytes with `targetDestSize` = 1, 13, 100, 4096, 12000 per block. Assert per-block `*srcSizePtr` bytes consumed, the whole stream decodes with `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`, and that a failing block leaves the stream usable (or marks it dirty). | [ ] |\n| 83 | `LZ4_saveDictHC`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | `LZ4_saveDictHC` clamping (lz4hc.c:1748-1750): after a 100 KB HC stream, save with dictSize = 0, 1, 3 (→ 0), 4, 1024, 65535, 65536, 65537, 200000 (→ 64 KB), and one value > the live `prefixSize` (→ clamped to prefixSize). `safeBuffer = NULL` with dictSize 0. Then continue with one more 8 KB block out of a fresh buffer and round-trip the whole stream. Levels 2, 9, 12. | [ ] |\n| 84 | `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`, `LZ4_loadDictHC` | Index-overflow re-base path (lz4hc.c:1695-1699, `(end-prefixStart) + dictLimit > 2 GB`): drive `dictLimit` high by many blocks (or by repeated `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast`, which adds `end-prefixStart` to `dictLimit` each time), then compress one more block and assert the stream silently re-loads the last 64 KB as dictionary and still round-trips. Also `LZ4HC_init_internal`'s `newStartingOffset > 1 GB → LZ4HC_clearTables` branch (lz4hc.c:248-251). | [ ] |\n| 85 | `LZ4_resetStreamHC`, `LZ4_compress_HC_continue` | `LZ4_resetStreamHC(s, level)` is a full `LZ4_initStreamHC` + `LZ4_setCompressionLevel`. After compressing a 40 KB stream at level 12, reset to levels 1, 2, 3, 9, 12, 0 (→9), 99 (→12) and compress the same first block: output must equal a freshly created stream at the same level. | [ ] |\n| 86 | `LZ4_compressHC`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput`, `LZ4_compress_HC` | Deprecated level-0 wrappers (level 0 → clamps to `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT` = 9). `LZ4_compressHC(src,dst,srcSize)` must equal `LZ4_compress_HC(src,dst,srcSize,LZ4_compressBound(srcSize),0)`; `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput` must equal `LZ4_compress_HC(...,maxDstSize,0)`. srcSize = 0, 1, 12, 13, 4096, 65547, 200000; maxDstSize = bound, exact, exact-1, 0. | [ ] |\n| 87 | `LZ4_compressHC2`, `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput` | Deprecated explicit-level wrappers. cLevel sweep = `INT_MIN`, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, `INT_MAX`. srcSize = 13, 4096, 40000; for `_limitedOutput` also maxDstSize = bound, exact, exact-1. Must equal `LZ4_compress_HC` with the same level. | [ ] |\n| 88 | `LZ4_compressHC_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC2_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_withStateHC` | Deprecated with-state wrappers, all four. State buffer of exactly `LZ4_sizeofStateHC()` bytes, aligned; the `HC_` pair hard-co