).\n\n## Entry points to cover — read lz4hc.h and cover ALL of these\n\nCurrent one-shot / state:\n- `LZ4_compress_HC(src, dst, srcSize, dstCapacity, compressionLevel)`\n- `LZ4_sizeofStateHC()` (compare the value between C and Rust)\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC(state, src, dst, srcSize, dstCapacity, level)`\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset(...)` — reuse the SAME state across several\n  successive calls, since that is precisely what differs from the full-reset variant, and\n  byte-compare the state blob after each call\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize(stateHC, src, dst, *srcSizePtr, targetDstSize, level)` —\n  sweep targetDstSize from 0/1/tiny up to more than enough; compare the returned value\n  AND the mutated `*srcSizePtr` out-parameter AND the output bytes\n\nStreaming:\n- `LZ4_createStreamHC` / `LZ4_freeStreamHC` / `LZ4_initStreamHC(buffer, size)` /\n  `LZ4_resetStreamHC(streamPtr, level)` / `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast(streamPtr, level)`\n- `LZ4_setCompressionLevel(streamPtr, level)` — including changing the level MID-STREAM\n  between blocks\n- `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed(streamPtr, favor)` with favor 0 and 1 (only meaningful at\n  level >= 10, but test it at low levels too)\n- `LZ4_loadDictHC(streamPtr, dict, dictSize)` — dict sizes 0, 1, 4, 100, 4096, 65535,\n  65536, 70000 (>64KB triggers truncation to the last 64KB)\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_continue(streamPtr, src, dst, srcSize, maxDstSize)` — multi-block\n  sequences of 2..8 blocks, with varying block sizes including blocks smaller than\n  MINMATCH and blocks larger than 64KB\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_continue_destSize(streamPtr, src, dst, *srcSizePtr, targetDstSize)`\n- `LZ4_saveDictHC(streamPtr, safeBuffer, maxDictSize)` — compare the return value AND the\n  bytes written into safeBuffer; use maxDictSize values 0, 100, 65536, and > 65536\n- `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary(working_stream, dictionary_stream)` — build a dictionary\n  stream with loadDictHC then attach it and compress; compare output\n- `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` is exported — inspect its C signature in lz4hc.c and call it\n  directly through the FFI with valid arguments if it is feasible to set up; if setting up\n  its arguments safely is not feasible, cover it indirectly via the extDict streaming path\n  (loadDictHC + compress_HC_continue with a separate dictionary buffer) and say so in a\n  comment.\n\nDeprecated / legacy (ALL are exported and MUST be exercised at least once each):\n- `LZ4_compressHC`, `LZ4_compressHC2`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput`,\n  `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput`, `LZ4_compressHC_withStateHC`,\n  `LZ4_compressHC2_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_withStateHC`,\n  `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_withStateHC`, `LZ4_compressHC_continue`,\n  `LZ4_compressHC2_continue`, `LZ4_compressHC_limitedOutput_continue`,\n  `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_continue`, `LZ4_createHC`, `LZ4_freeHC`,\n  `LZ4_slideInputBufferHC`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamStateHC`, `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC`\n  Read their exact signatures out of `lz4hc.h` / `lz4hc.c` — several take a `char*` state\n  or return `void*`. Get them right.\n\n## Input shapes\nFor every level regime, sweep sizes 0,1,4,5,12,13,16,63,64,65,255,256,1000,4096,65535,\n65536,65546,65547,65548,100000,200000 and all `N_SHAPES` data shapes. Include highly\nrepetitive data (forces very long matches and the optimal parser's long-match paths) and\nrandom data (forces literal runs). Add a randomized property loop with a fixed seed.\n\n## Round-trip validation\nFor each compressed output, also decompress with `LZ4_decompress_safe` (from BOTH libs)\nand assert the result equals the original input — HC output must be valid LZ4 block data.\n\n## Error paths (Phase C) — put these in the SAME file\nGrep lz4hc.c for every failure return and test each, asserting C and Rust return the\nIDENTICAL value:\n- `srcSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` behaviour (do NOT actually allocate 2 GB — instead find\n  whether the check is on the size argument only, and if you can pass a large size with a\n  small buffer safely, do; otherwise SKIP and note it in a comment. Never cause a segfault.)\n- `dstCapacity` too small: 0, 1, and every size from 1 up to just below the minimum\n  needed — the limitedOutput path must return 0 identically\n- `LZ4_initStreamHC` with a buffer that is too SMALL, and with a MISALIGNED buffer\n  (use `AlignedBuf::with_offset(size, 8, 1)`) — must return NULL identically\n- `LZ4_compress_HC` with `dstCapacity` 0\n- out-of-range compression levels (already in the level list above)\n- `LZ4_setCompressionLevel` with out-of-range levels, then compress and compare\n\n## Deliverable\n\nWrite ONE file: `tests/lz4hc_diff.rs`.\n\nThen run it and make it PASS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4hc_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nUse `--release --offline`. If a test reveals a genuine divergence, FIX `src/lz4hc.rs` to\nmatch the C exactly, then `timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running\n(the test loads the built `.so`). Keep total runtime under ~180 seconds; HC level 12 on\n200 KB inputs is slow, so scale iteration counts sensibly while KEEPING full axis coverage.\n\nReport back: the exact list of `#[test]` function names, the final pass/fail line, any\ndivergences found and how you fixed the Rust, and confirm every exported lz4hc symbol\nlisted above is exercised.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ieCE1Y-translated-rust/5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b/tasks/a066b9b93579961ef.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
