{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kgatrodhlwflkr4zmlvl32gghomb67tl5cnhzwplzxxghs544z3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Written to `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/CONFIGS_part1.md`.\n\n## Totals\n\n| section | rows | numbers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `## lz4.c — block API` | 62 | 1–62 |\n| `## lz4hc.c — HC API` | 31 | 63–93 |\n| `## xxhash.c` | 22 | 94–115 |\n| **total** | **115** | globally sequential 1–115, verified |\n\n## Symbol coverage\n\nVerified mechanically against `SYMBOLS.md`: all **104** symbols owned by `lz4.c` (50), `lz4hc.c` (35), and `xxhash.c` (19) appear in the **entry point(s)** column of at least one row. **Zero missing.** (The remaining 39 exported symbols belong to `lz4frame.c`/`lz4file.c`, which are out of scope for this task.)\n\n## Corrections to the task brief that the source forced\n\nThese matter for anyone implementing the rows:\n\n1. **`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` is 2, not 3** (`lz4hc.h:47`), and there are **three** HC strategies, not two. `k_clTable` (lz4hc.c:92–106) maps levels 1–2 → **`lz4mid`** (`LZ4MID_compress`, an entirely separate compressor with dual 4-byte/8-byte hash tables), 3–9 → `lz4hc` (`LZ4HC_compress_hashChain`), 10–12 → `lz4opt` (`LZ4HC_compress_optimal`). The brief only asked for hashChain + optimal; `lz4mid` is a third full code path with its own `_dest_overflow` / fillOutput handling and its own dictionary filler (`LZ4MID_fillHTable`) and ext-dict searcher (`LZ4MID_searchExtDict`). Rows 65, 73, 75, 77, 80, 81 cover it.\n2. **`cLevel < 1` clamps to 9, not to `CLEVEL_MIN`** (`LZ4HC_getCLevelParams`, lz4hc.c:112). So level 0 (used by all the deprecated `LZ4_compressHC*` wrappers) behaves as level 9, while level 1 stays at 1 and lands in `lz4mid`.\n3. **`patternAnalysis` is on only at level 9** (`nbSearches > 128`), and **`fullUpdate` only at level 12** — these are sub-axes inside the hash-chain/optimal paths that levels 3–8 and 10–11 do not exercise. Split into rows 66/67 and 68.\n4. **`favorDecSpeed` is only forwarded to `LZ4HC_compress_optimal`** (lz4hc.c:1393–1410), so it is a no-op at levels 1–9. Row 69 asserts both the effect (10–12) and the non-effect (2, 9).\n5. **`byPtr` is unreachable on a 64-bit build.** Every selection site is `((sizeof(void*)==4) && ((uptrval)src > LZ4_DISTANCE_MAX)) ? byPtr : byU32`. Row 24 records this explicitly and gates it on a 32-bit build; `clearedTable` (the 4th `tableType_t`) is covered separately in rows 4/6/23.\n6. **`LZ4_64Klimit` is 65547**, not 65536 — the byU16/byU32 switch is at `srcSize >= 65547`, so the interesting boundary pair is 65546/65547 (row 14), not 65535/65536.\n7. **`checkOffset` in the decoder is `dictSize < 64KB`** (lz4.c:2047), so `dictSize == 65535` and `65536` take *different* decoder paths — folded into row 55.\n8. `LZ4_compressHC2_continue` / `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_continue` call `LZ4HC_compress_generic` **directly**, bypassing auto-init, `LZ4HC_setExternalDict` and the 2 GB overflow check that every other `_continue` entry point performs (row 90) — they require a context prepared via `LZ4_createHC`/`LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` (row 91).\n9. `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState_internal` leaves the stream in a broken state; only the public `_extState` wrapper re-runs `LZ4_initStream` on exit (row 28).\n10. `LZ4HC_encodeSequence` emits match-length continuations in **510-byte steps** (`{255;255;}`) unlike lz4.c's 4×255 `LZ4_write32(0xFFFFFFFF)` loop — different byte-emission code for the same format, so HC and non-HC long-match encodings must be tested separately (row 92)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":310,"cache_read_input_tokens":196964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014iwpBoykox5