{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hbxefleqlmo5bfmvqnz7qpybacqhaqiu6dgnebfdl7ry3m4asela","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrote `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/ERRORS_part1.md`.\n\n## Row counts\n- **Total: 167 rows**, globally sequential (verified programmatically, no gaps)\n- `## lz4.c` — **93 rows** (#1–93)\n- `## lz4hc.c` — **54 rows** (#94–147)\n- `## xxhash.c` — **20 rows** (#148–167)\n\nIt's above the 40–70 estimate because I split every distinct branch *and* every distinct testable trigger value of a shared branch (e.g. `srcSize < 0` vs `srcSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` at lz4.c:1360), and because clamps and assert-only/no-check paths were requested as rows too.\n\n## Key findings worth flagging to the caller\n- **`offset == 0` in a compressed block is NOT rejected by any decoder.** Neither `match + dictSize < lowPrefix` (lz4.c:2161/2356) nor `offset > (op-prefixStart)+dictSize` (lz4.c:1926) catches it; the decoder zero-fills via `LZ4_write32(op, 0)` and returns a positive length. This is a common false assumption — row 62 documents the real behaviour, and the Rust port must not error here.\n- **Alignment/NULL-state handling is inconsistent between lz4 and lz4hc.** `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC*` explicitly `return 0` for misaligned/NULL state (lz4hc.c:1503, 1515), whereas `LZ4_compress_fast_extState` (lz4.c:1384-1385) and `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState` (lz4.c:1483-1484) have only `assert()` and are UB in release. Rows 24-25 / 104-108.\n- **`LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` returns 1 on error, not 0** (lz4hc.c:2153) — inverted convention vs every other function.\n- **`notLimited` split is a real error-surface hole**: when `dstCapacity >= LZ4_compressBound(srcSize)`, all output-overflow checks are compiled out, so a lying capacity overflows `dst` and never returns 0 (rows 13-14, 131-132; `LZ4_compressHC2_continue` hard-codes `dstCapacity = 0` with `notLimited`).\n- **`LZ4_decompress_fast*` has zero input-side validation** (`read_long_length_no_check`, lz4.c:1852) — only the five output-side `-1` checks exist (rows 73-78).\n- **xxhash NULL handling**: only `XXH32/64_update` validate anything (`input == NULL` → `XXH_ERROR`, because `XXH_ACCEPT_NULL_INPUT_POINTER == 0`). `reset`, `copyState`, `digest`, `canonicalFromHash`, `hashFromCanonical`, and `XXH32/64(NULL, len>0, seed)` have no checks at all; `freeState(NULL)` returns `XXH_OK`. Also `XXH32_update`'s `total_len_32` silently wraps past 4 GiB (row 151).\n- Silent clamps that tests must assert on rather than treat as errors: acceleration (1 / 65537), HC level (9 / 12), `LZ4_saveDict`/`LZ4_saveDictHC`/`LZ4_loadDict*` 64 KB truncation, `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` 16-byte floor, `LZ4_compress_destSize`/`_HC_destSize` input truncation with `*srcSizePtr` rewritten."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":204544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":428,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01G5uiYWf5DTz4MUr2vgJvH9","session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"59c1f7a7-a3e3-4764-8de4-e65a491c9bf3","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:14:08.984Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"ERRORS table for lz4/lz4hc/xxhash"}
