{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pxb5bqphazsnsubvnmkaajajvwqkyswfti34ttkxzb2r3cbdulwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01KBd4WdpnxbaghnJyS6gKhH","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Write lz4frame compression tests","prompt":"Write Rust differential integration tests for the COMPRESSION side of lz4frame.c in an LZ4 C-to-Rust translation.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\n## Context\n- `c_src/src/lz4frame.c` + `c_src/include/lz4frame.h` + `c_src/include/lz4frame_static.h`\n  are the C ground truth. `src/lz4frame.rs` is the Rust translation.\n- The C is ALWAYS correct. If outputs diverge, FIX THE RUST (`src/lz4frame.rs`), never the C.\n  DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`.\n- Already built: C = `c_src/build/liblz4.so`, Rust = `target/release/liblz4.so`.\n\n## MANDATORY: use the existing harness\nREAD `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST, and read `tests/lz4_stream.rs` as a worked example of\nthe required style. The harness provides:\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way to obtain functions.\n  NEVER call Rust code directly, never `use lz4::...`. All calls go through the `.so`\n  export tables via libloading so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are tested too.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`: `next_u64`, `next_u32`, `byte`, `below(n)`, `range(lo,hi)`, `bool()`\n- `gen_shape(&mut rng, shape, len)`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name(shape)`\n- `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c_bytes, rust_bytes)`\n- Already-defined `#[repr(C)]` types: `LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, `LZ4F_preferences_t`\n  (both have `Default` impls mirroring `LZ4F_INIT_FRAMEINFO` / `LZ4F_INIT_PREFERENCES`),\n  `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_CustomMem`\n- Constants: `LZ4F_default`(0), `LZ4F_max64KB`(4), `LZ4F_max256KB`(5), `LZ4F_max1MB`(6),\n  `LZ4F_max4MB`(7), `LZ4F_blockLinked`(0), `LZ4F_blockIndependent`(1),\n  `LZ4F_noContentChecksum`(0), `LZ4F_contentChecksumEnabled`(1),\n  `LZ4F_noBlockChecksum`(0), `LZ4F_blockChecksumEnabled`(1), `LZ4F_frame`(0),\n  `LZ4F_skippableFrame`(1), `LZ4F_VERSION`(100), `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MIN/MAX`,\n  `LZ4F_MAGICNUMBER`, `LZ4F_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START`\n- `lz4f_is_error(code) -> bool` and `lz4f_error_code(code) -> i32` replicating\n  `LZ4F_isError` / `LZ4F_getErrorCode`, plus the `err::` module with every\n  `LZ4F_ERROR_*` numeric value (e.g. `err::ERROR_dstMaxSize_tooSmall` == 11).\n- **HARNESS RULE**: pre-fill the C dst buffer and the Rust dst buffer with the SAME\n  sentinel byte (`0xAA`), then compare the FULL buffer. Different fills give false\n  positives on untouched bytes.\n\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\nRemember `size_t` == `usize` in these signatures, and `LZ4F_cctx*`/`LZ4F_CDict*` are\nopaque — model them as `*mut c_void`.\n\n## Entry points you own (COMPRESSION side) — cover ALL of them\n- `LZ4F_getVersion`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`, `LZ4F_getBlockSize`\n- `LZ4F_isError`, `LZ4F_getErrorName` (compare the returned C string bytes for EVERY\n  error code 0..=24 AND for several out-of-range codes)\n- `LZ4F_getErrorCode` for many `size_t` inputs including 0, small successes, and every\n  `-(size_t)code`\n- `LZ4F_compressFrameBound(srcSize, prefsPtr)` — with NULL prefs and with every\n  preference combination; sweep srcSize widely\n- `LZ4F_compressBound(srcSize, prefsPtr)` — same sweep, NULL prefs included\n- `LZ4F_compressFrame(dst, dstCapacity, src, srcSize, prefsPtr)` — the one-shot\n- `LZ4F_createCompressionContext(&ctx, version)` / `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext(ctx)`\n- `LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced(customMem, version)` — pass\n  `LZ4F_CustomMem::default()` (all-NULL == defer to stdlib)\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, prefsPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_internal` — read its exact signature in lz4frame.c and call it\n  directly through the FFI\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, src, srcSize, cOptPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, src, srcSize, cOptPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_flush(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, cOptPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, cOptPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_createCDict(dictBuffer, dictSize)` / `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced(customMem, dict, size)`\n  / `LZ4F_freeCDict(cdict)`\n- `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, src, srcSize, cdict, prefsPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, cdict, prefsPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict(ctx, dst, dstCapacity, dictBuffer, dictSize, prefsPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce(...)` — read exact signature from the header/source\nVerify each signature against the C source before using it.\n\n## Preference axes to sweep (the cross-product, pruned sensibly)\n- `blockSizeID`: 0(default), 4, 5, 6, 7\n- `blockMode`: blockLinked, blockIndependent\n- `contentChecksumFlag`: 0, 1\n- `blockChecksumFlag`: 0, 1\n- `frameType`: LZ4F_frame, LZ4F_skippableFrame\n- `contentSize`: 0 (field omitted) and the exact srcSize (8-byte field written)\n- `dictID`: 0 (omitted) and non-zero values incl. 0xFFFFFFFF\n- `compressionLevel`: i32::MIN, -65537, -100, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13,\n  100, i32::MAX.  **CRITICAL**: lz4frame picks LZ4-fast vs LZ4HC by\n  `level < LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN`, and LZ4HC itself has THREE strategies\n  (levels 1-2 -> `lz4mid`, 3-9 -> hashChain, 10-12 -> optimal), so all regimes must be hit.\n- `autoFlush`: 0, 1\n- `favorDecSpeed`: 0, 1\n- `LZ4F_compressOptions_t.stableSrc`: 0, 1\n\n## Input shape / call-pattern axes\n- srcSize: 0, 1, 2, a few bytes, blockSize-1, blockSize, blockSize+1, 2*blockSize,\n  several whole blocks, many blocks, and sizes far larger than blockSize\n  (compute blockSize from `LZ4F_getBlockSize(blockSizeID)`)\n- all `N_SHAPES` data shapes — random data forces the \"stored/uncompressed block\"\n  path where the block-header high bit is set; repetitive data forces long matches\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` driven with MANY chunk patterns over the same total input:\n  one big chunk; byte-at-a-time; fixed chunks 1,2,3,7,16,100,1000; chunk sizes that\n  land EXACTLY on the block boundary and one byte either side; RANDOM chunk sizes.\n  This is what drives the internal `tmpBuff`/`tmpIn`/`tmpInSize` buffering paths.\n- interleave `LZ4F_flush` between updates, both with autoFlush=0 and autoFlush=1\n- `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` (only valid with blockIndependent): alone, and MIXED with\n  `LZ4F_compressUpdate` so buffered compressed data must be flushed first\n- CDict / dict axes: dict sizes 0, 1, 100, 4096, 65535, 65536, 70000 (>64KB truncation)\n\n## What to assert\nFor every configuration: call BOTH libraries and assert\n1. identical return values from every single call, and\n2. byte-identical output buffers (full buffer, same sentinel prefill), and\n3. for the full-pipeline rows, that the C-produced frame and Rust-produced frame are\n   byte-identical AND that the frame decompresses back to the original input (use\n   `LZ4F_decompress` from both libs for the round-trip check).\n\n## Deliverable\nWrite ONE file: `tests/lz4frame_compress_diff.rs`.\n\nThen make it PASS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4frame_compress_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nAlways use `--release --offline`. Other agents may be building concurrently, so if cargo\nblocks on the target lock, just wait / retry. After ANY edit to `src/lz4frame.rs`, run\n`timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running the test (the test loads\nthe built `.so`).\n\nKeep total runtime under ~180 seconds — 4 MB block sizes and HC level 12 are slow, so\nscale iteration counts sensibly while KEEPING full axis coverage.\n\nReport back: exact `#[test]` function names, the final pass/fail line, every divergence\nyou found with the precise C-vs-Rust difference and how you fixed the Rust, and confirm\nwhich of the listed symbols you exercised."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":569,"cache_read_input_tokens":155190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":569,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"db5cb07d-a7b3-4c7b-91c2-0ec3642eb00c","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:17:09.857Z"}
