{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_b3sq4vhg227o3s4st32twq6abd52nd7t3wuc2xuc2jnodn4izrhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01VCLqGkeKkfyy1T3KvQHd9f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/CONFIGS_part2.md","content":"# CONFIGS_part2 — Valid-configuration surface for differential testing (lz4frame.c / lz4file.c)\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/src/lz4frame.c` (2136 lines) and `c_src/src/lz4file.c` (341 lines).\nEvery row is a *valid* input configuration (the mirror image of an error table): the C is expected to\nsucceed (or return a well-defined result) and the Rust port must produce byte-identical output and an\nidentical return value.\n\n## Axes the C actually branches on (derived from source)\n\n| axis | values the code distinguishes | where |\n|---|---|---|\n| `blockSizeID` | `0`→remapped to `LZ4F_max64KB`; `4`=64 KB, `5`=256 KB, `6`=1 MB, `7`=4 MB | `LZ4F_getBlockSize` L333-342; remap also at `LZ4F_compressBegin_internal` L738-740 |\n| `LZ4F_optimalBSID` | shrinks the requested ID based on `srcSize` — **only** on the `LZ4F_compressFrame*` path; `requested==0` is returned unchanged (loop body never runs) | L359-371, called L448 |\n| `blockMode` | `LZ4F_blockLinked` vs `LZ4F_blockIndependent`; selects `*_continue` vs one-shot compress fn; controls `tmpBuff` sizing (`+64 KB` / `+128 KB`) and decoder `tmpOutBuffer` sizing (`+128 KB`); `LZ4F_compressFrame*` **force-downgrades to blockIndependent when `srcSize <= blockSize`** | L742-744, L759-762, L952-962, L450-451, L1680-1681 |\n| `contentChecksumFlag` | 0 / 1 → 4-byte XXH32 suffix; decoder `dstage_getSuffix`/`storeSuffix` | L1100-1101, L1225-1231, L1983-2030 |\n| `blockChecksumFlag` | 0 / 1 → 4-byte XXH32 **of the compressed/stored block bytes** after each block; two *different* decode paths: `dstage_getBlockChecksum` for stored blocks, inline check in `getCBlock` for compressed blocks | L903-906, L1744-1746/L1803-1837, L1871-1883 |\n| `frameType` | `LZ4F_frame` (magic `0x184D2204`) vs `LZ4F_skippableFrame` (magic `0x184D2A50..0x184D2A5F`, i.e. `magic & 0xFFFFFFF0 == LZ4F_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START`) — decode-only | L1358-1368, L1452-1454, L2032-2077 |\n| `contentSize` | `0` → field omitted (FLG bit3 clear, header 7/11 bytes); `!=0` → 8-byte LE field, `totalInSize` reset, `LZ4F_compressEnd` validates → `frameSize_wrong`; decoder tracks `frameRemainingSize` | L790, L796-800, L1235-1238, L1428-1430, L1776-1777, L1984 |\n| `dictID` | `0` → omitted; `!=0` → FLG bit0 + 4-byte LE field | L792, L802-805, L1431-1432 |\n| `compressionLevel` | **`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN == 2` in this tree** (not 3). `< 2` → LZ4 fast (`acceleration = level<0 ? -level+1 : 1`); `>= 2` → LZ4HC; `2..9` hashChain; `>= LZ4HC_CLEVEL_OPT_MIN(10)` optimal parser; `12 == LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX`; `> 12` clamped to 12; `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT == 9` | L502/L519, L705, L711, L728-733, L763, L913, L925, L956, L967; `lz4hc.h` L47-50, `lz4hc.c` L113-114/L1614-1615 |\n| `autoFlush` | 0 → data buffered in `tmpBuff`, `requiredBuffSize = maxBlockSize + (linked?128KB:0)`; 1 → partial tail block emitted immediately, `requiredBuffSize = linked?64KB:0`. Also gates the \"keep tmpIn within limits\" `LZ4F_localSaveDict` branch, and `LZ4F_compressBound`'s `alreadyBuffered` | L742-744, L1057-1066, L1082-1090, L869-872 |\n| `favorDecSpeed` | 0 / 1; only applied when `compressionLevel >= LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` | L763-765 |\n| `stableSrc` | 0 → `LZ4F_localSaveDict` into `tmpBuff`, `tmpIn = tmpBuff + realDictSize`; 1 → `tmpIn = tmpBuff` (history stays in caller's src). Only reached for `blockLinked && lastBlockCompressed==fromSrcBuffer`. `LZ4F_compressFrame*` forces `stableSrc=1` | L1069-1079, L453-454 |\n| `stableDst` | 0 → post-loop history copy into `tmpOutBuffer`; 1 → skipped | L2083-2111 |\n| `skipChecksums` | sticky OR-ed into `dctx->skipChecksum`; once 1, disabled for rest of frame | L1638, L1769-1775, L1821, L1906, L1951, L2016 |\n| block compress mode | `LZ4B_COMPRESSED` (`LZ4F_compressUpdate`) vs `LZ4B_UNCOMPRESSED` (`LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` → `LZ4F_doNotCompressBlock` → always stored). Switching mode mid-frame triggers an implicit `LZ4F_flush` of the buffered block **in the old mode** | L1009-1017, L946-955, L1173 |\n| stored-block trigger | `LZ4F_makeBlock`: `cSize == 0 || cSize >= srcSize` → write `srcSize | LZ4F_BLOCKUNCOMPRESSED_FLAG` and `memcpy` the raw bytes. Incompressible data hits this naturally (dstCapacity passed to the compressor is `srcSize-1`) | L892-902 |\n| decoder `dStage` | `getFrameHeader`, `storeFrameHeader`, `init`, `getBlockHeader`, `storeBlockHeader`, `copyDirect`, `getBlockChecksum`, `getCBlock`, `storeCBlock`, `flushOut`, `getSuffix`, `storeSuffix`, `getSFrameSize`, `storeSFrameSize`, `skipSkippable` (15 states; there is **no** separate `decodeCBlock`/`decodeCBlock_intoTmp` state — the in-dst vs in-tmpOut choice is a branch inside `getCBlock`/`storeCBlock`) | L1248-1258, L1644-2078 |\n| decode dst sizing | `(dstEnd-dstPtr) >= maxBlockSize` **and** `!(dict != NULL && dict+dictSize == tmpOut)` → decode straight into dst; otherwise decode into `tmpOut` then `dstage_flushOut` | L1886-1890, L1921-1958 |\n| header length | `7` (no contentSize, no dictID) / `11` (dictID only) / `15` (contentSize only) / `19` (both). `LZ4F_compressBegin*` still requires `dstCapacity >= 19` in every case | L700, L1394, L1462-1467 |\n| 19-byte decode shortcut | `dstage_getFrameHeader` takes the direct-decode shortcut only when `srcEnd-srcPtr >= maxFHSize(19)`; fewer bytes → `dstage_storeFrameHeader`. A whole tiny frame (< 19 bytes) therefore exercises the store path even in a single call | L1649-1673 |\n| lz4file `blockSizeID` switch | `LZ4F_readOpen` / `LZ4F_writeOpen` each have their **own** `switch` mapping `LZ4F_default`→64 KB, 4→64 KB, 5→256 KB, 6→1 MB, 7→4 MB; `prefsPtr == NULL` in `writeOpen` → 64 KB. `readOpen` always `fread`s exactly 19 bytes and fails `io_read` if the file is shorter | `lz4file.c` L95-99, L108-125, L229-250 |\n\n## Data generators referenced by the rows\n\n* `RUN(n)` — `n` bytes all `0x41`. Maximally compressible (long runs).\n* `TEXT(n)` — `n` bytes of the 64-byte ASCII pattern `\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789abcdef\\n\\t !\"` repeated/truncated. Realistically compressible with matches.\n* `RAND(n)` — `n` bytes from xorshift32 seeded `0x12345678` (`x^=x<<13; x^=x>>17; x^=x<<5;`, take low byte). Incompressible → forces stored blocks.\n* `MIX(n)` — first `n/2` bytes `RUN`, second `n/2` bytes `RAND`.\n* \"`INIT`\" — `LZ4F_INIT_PREFERENCES` = `{{LZ4F_max64KB, LZ4F_blockLinked, LZ4F_noContentChecksum, LZ4F_frame, 0, 0, LZ4F_noBlockChecksum}, 0, 0, 0, {0,0,0}}`.\n* Unless a row says otherwise, `dstCapacity` = `LZ4F_compressFrameBound(srcSize, prefs)` for one-shot calls and `LZ4F_compressBound(chunkSize, prefs)` for streaming calls, and every row asserts **byte-identical** output plus identical return value between C and Rust, and asserts the frame round-trips back to the original bytes.\n\n---\n\n## lz4frame.c — compression\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `LZ4F_getVersion`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max` | No inputs. Assert `LZ4F_getVersion() == 100` (`LZ4F_VERSION`) and `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max() == 12` (`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX`). | [ ] |\n| 2 | `LZ4F_isError`, `LZ4F_getErrorName`, `LZ4F_getErrorCode` | Sweep `code` over: `0`, `1`, `100`, `(size_t)-1` … `(size_t)-24` (every `LZ4F_errorCodes` value from `ERROR_GENERIC` to `ERROR_io_read`), and `(size_t)-25` (`-LZ4F_ERROR_maxCode`, the first value that is **not** an error). For each: compare `LZ4F_isError` (0/1), the exact NUL-terminated string returned by `LZ4F_getErrorName` (including `\"Unspecified error code\"` for non-errors), and the `LZ4F_getErrorCode` enum value. | [ ] |\n| 3 | `LZ4F_getBlockSize` | `blockSizeID` = `LZ4F_default(0)` → `65536`; `4` → `65536`; `5` → `262144`; `6` → `1048576`; `7` → `4194304`. One assert per value. | [ ] |\n| 4 | `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` | `preferencesPtr = NULL` (⇒ all-zero prefs: blockSizeID 0→64 KB, no checksums, `autoFlush` forced to 1 internally). `srcSize` ∈ {0, 1, 65535, 65536, 65537, 131072, 4194304}. Assert the exact returned size for each. | [ ] |\n| 5 | `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` | `prefs` = INIT + `blockSizeID` swept over 4/5/6/7 + `contentChecksumFlag = LZ4F_contentChecksumEnabled` + `blockChecksumFlag = LZ4F_blockChecksumEnabled` + `autoFlush = 0` (overridden to 1 inside) + `compressionLevel = 0`. For each blockSizeID, `srcSize` ∈ {0, 1, blockSize-1, blockSize, blockSize+1, 3×blockSize (exact multiple ⇒ `lastBlockSize==0`)}. | [ ] |\n| 6 | `LZ4F_compressBound` | `prefsPtr = NULL` ⇒ worst case: both checksum flags forced on, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `alreadyBuffered = (size_t)-1` ⇒ `bufferedSize = 65535`. `srcSize` ∈ {0, 1, 65535, 65536, 65537, 1048576}. | [ ] |\n| 7 | `LZ4F_compressBound` | `prefs` = INIT + `autoFlush = 1`, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max256KB`, `contentChecksumFlag = enabled`, `blockChecksumFlag = noBlockChecksum`. `srcSize` ∈ {0, 1, 262143, 262144, 262145}. (`alreadyBuffered = 0` branch.) | [ ] |\n| 8 | `LZ4F_compressBound` | `prefs` = INIT + `autoFlush = 0`, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max1MB`, `blockChecksumFlag = enabled`, `contentChecksumFlag = noContentChecksum`. `srcSize` ∈ {0, 1, 1048575, 1048576, 1048577}. (`alreadyBuffered = (size_t)-1` branch.) | [ ] |\n| 9 | `LZ4F_compressFrame` | `preferencesPtr = NULL`; `srcBuffer` non-NULL, `srcSize = 0`. Expect exactly 7-byte header + 4-byte zero endMark = 11 bytes. | [ ] |\n| 10 | `LZ4F_compressFrame` | `preferencesPtr = NULL`; `src = RUN(1)` (single `0x41`). One block; whole frame is 7 + 4 + cSize + 4 bytes (< 19 bytes total — this frame is reused as the decode fixture for the `dstage_storeFrameHeader` row). | [ ] |\n| 11 | `LZ4F_compressFrame` | `preferencesPtr = NULL`; `src = RAND(64)` — incompressible ⇒ `cSiz