→ `flush` → `compressUpdate(...)` → `compressEnd`. `dstCapacity` for each flush = `LZ4F_compressBound(0, &prefs)`. Assert `flush` return values and that `tmpIn += tmpInSize` keeps history contiguous (linked blocks reference earlier flushed data). | [ ] |\n| 61 | `LZ4F_flush` | (a) `compressBegin` then `LZ4F_flush` immediately, twice in a row, `dstCapacity = 0` — must return 0 both times (the `tmpInSize == 0` early return happens *before* the `cStage`/`dstCapacity` checks). (b) prefs with `autoFlush = 1`: interleave `flush` after every `compressUpdate` over 10 × 10000-byte chunks — every `flush` must return 0 because nothing is ever buffered. | [ ] |\n| 62 | `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_flush`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | prefs = INIT + `blockMode = LZ4F_blockLinked`, `compressionLevel = 9`, `blockChecksumFlag = enabled`, `autoFlush = 0`, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`. `compressUpdate(TEXT(30000))` (all buffered), then `LZ4F_flush` with `dstCapacity` **exactly** `30000 + 4 + 4 = 30008` (the minimum the code accepts). Then `compressEnd`. Covers `LZ4F_compressBlockHC_continue` reached through `flush`'s own `LZ4F_selectCompression(..., cctx->blockCompressMode)`. | [ ] |\n| 63 | `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | prefs = INIT + `blockMode = LZ4F_blockIndependent` (required), `autoFlush = 1`, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `level = 0`; **one** `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` with `TEXT(200000)`, `dstCapacity = max(srcSize, LZ4F_compressBound(200000,&prefs))`. `LZ4F_doNotCompressBlock` returns 0 ⇒ every block written stored (`size | 0x80000000`). 3 full blocks + 3392-byte tail. | [ ] |\n| 64 | `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | prefs = INIT + `blockIndependent`, `autoFlush = 0`, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `blockChecksumFlag = enabled`; 200 × 1000-byte `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` calls over `TEXT(200000)` ⇒ buffering through `tmpBuff` then stored blocks + per-block CRC over the raw bytes; `compressEnd` flushes the tail. | [ ] |\n| 65 | `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate`, `LZ4F_flush`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | prefs = INIT + `blockMode = LZ4F_blockIndependent`, `autoFlush = 0`, `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `level = 0`. Sequence, all with `cOptPtr = NULL` and `dstCapacity = LZ4F_compressBound(20000,&prefs)`: `compressUpdate(TEXT(1000))` (buffered, mode `LZ4B_COMPRESSED`) → `uncompressedUpdate(TEXT(1000))` (mode change ⇒ implicit `LZ4F_flush` emits the buffered 1000 bytes as a **compressed** block, then buffers uncompressed) → `compressUpdate(TEXT(1000))` (mode change back ⇒ implicit flush emits the buffered 1000 bytes as a **stored** block) → `uncompressedUpdate(srcBuffer, 0)` (zero-size, mode change with empty buffer ⇒ flush returns 0) → `compressEnd`. Assert the resulting frame alternates compressed/stored block headers in exactly that order. | [ ] |\n| 66 | `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_compressEnd`, `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext` | **cctx reuse across compression-level regimes**: one cctx, three consecutive frames with `TEXT(70000)` each. Frame 1 `compressionLevel = 1` (`ctxTypeID = 1`, `lz4CtxAlloc = 0` ⇒ allocates `LZ4_stream_t`); frame 2 `compressionLevel = 9` (`ctxTypeID = 2`, `allocatedSize < requiredSize` ⇒ frees and allocates `LZ4_streamHC_t`); frame 3 `compressionLevel = 1` again (`allocatedSize >= requiredSize` but `lz4CtxType != ctxTypeID` ⇒ in-place `LZ4_initStream` on the HC-sized buffer). Assert frame 1 and frame 3 are byte-identical. | [ ] |\n| 67 | `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | **cctx reuse across `blockSizeID`/`autoFlush`**: one cctx. Frame 1: `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max4MB`, `autoFlush = 0`, `blockLinked` ⇒ `tmpBuff` = 4 MB + 128 KB. Frame 2: `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `autoFlush = 0`, `blockLinked` ⇒ `requiredBuffSize` = 64 KB + 128 KB `< maxBufferSize` ⇒ buffer **not** reallocated/shrunk, so the \"keep tmpIn within limits\" branch has far more headroo