etDecompressionContext`, `LZ4F_decompress` | Fixture pair: decode the first 2 blocks of the #21 (4 MB blockLinked) frame, abort, `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext`, then decode the **whole** #12 frame (64 KB blockIndependent) with the *same* dctx. Reset clears `dStage`/`dict`/`dictSize`/`skipChecksum`/`frameRemainingSize` but **not** `frameInfo`, `maxBlockSize`, `maxBufferSize`, `tmpIn`, `tmpOutBuffer` — so the second decode reuses the 4 MB + 128 KB buffers. Assert exact output and returned hints. | [ ] |\n| 72 | `LZ4F_headerSize` | Frames from #44's four header shapes. For each: `srcSize = 5` exactly (`LZ4F_MIN_SIZE_TO_KNOW_HEADER_LENGTH`), `srcSize = 7`, and `srcSize = 19`. Expect 7 / 11 / 15 / 19 respectively, independent of `srcSize`. Also `srcSize` larger than the whole frame. | [ ] |\n| 73 | `LZ4F_headerSize` | Skippable-frame magic sweep: `src` = LE32 of each of the 16 values `0x184D2A50 .. 0x184D2A5F` followed by an arbitrary LE32 size and payload; `srcSize = 5` and `srcSize = 8`. Every one must return `8`. Also assert `0x184D2A4F` and `0x184D2A60` are *not* treated as skippable (they fall through to the magic check). | [ ] |\n| 74 | `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` | Called **before** any `LZ4F_decompress`, on a fresh dctx, for each of #44's four header shapes plus the #26 (blockChecksum) / #25 (contentChecksum) / #30 (all fields, max4MB) fixtures. Two sub-cases per fixture: `*srcSizePtr = 19` (more than needed) and `*srcSizePtr = ` the exact header size. Assert every field of the returned `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` (`blockSizeID`, `blockMode`, `contentChecksumFlag`, `frameType == LZ4F_frame`, `contentSize`, `dictID`, `blockChecksumFlag`), that `*srcSizePtr` was updated to the header size, and that the return value is `4` (`LZ4F_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE`). | [ ] |\n| 75 | `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`, `LZ4F_decompress` | **Mid-stream** call: fixture #25. First `LZ4F_decompress` the whole frame *except* the last 10 bytes into a large dst (so `dStage > dstage_storeFrameHeader`), then `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`. Assert `*srcSizePtr == 0`, `frameInfoPtr` matches, and the return value is exactly what `LZ4F_decompress(dctx, NULL, &0, NULL, &0, NULL)` yields (the internal zero-length re-entry into the state machine with `dstBuffer == NULL`). Repeat with the pause landing in `dstage_flushOut` (use a small dst) and in `dstage_getBlockHeader`. | [ ] |\n| 76 | `LZ4F_getFrameInfo`, `LZ4F_decompress` | `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` first with `*srcSizePtr = 19`, then resume `LZ4F_decompress` from `srcBuffer + *srcSizePtr` for the remainder of the frame in one call. Fixtures: #30 (19-byte header) and #10 (7-byte header). Assert full, correct decompression and the hint sequence. | [ ] |\n| 77 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **One call, whole frame, `dOptPtr = NULL`**: for each fixture #9 (empty), #11 (stored), #15, #17, #19, #21, #22, #25, #26, #27, #28, #30. `*srcSizePtr` = full frame size (≥ 19 ⇒ `dstage_getFrameHeader` shortcut), `*dstSizePtr` = exact original content size. Assert `*srcSizePtr`/`*dstSizePtr` fully consumed/produced, return value `0` (frame complete), and byte-exact output. | [ ] |\n| 78 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **Tiny frame in a single call**: fixture #10 (total frame length < 19 bytes) and fixture #9 (11 bytes). Because `srcEnd - srcPtr < maxFHSize`, the code cannot take the shortcut and must go `dstage_getFrameHeader → dstage_storeFrameHeader` (copying into `dctx->header`, `tmpInTarget = 7`) even though all bytes are available. Assert full decode in one call and return `0`. Also feed `*srcSizePtr = 0` first ⇒ must return `minFHSize == 7` with nothing consumed. | [ ] |\n| 79 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **1 byte of src per call**, `dst` large (≥ `maxBlockSize`). Fixture #15 (`blockSizeID = max64KB`, `blockLinked`, no checksums, 4 blocks, 7-byte header). Drives `getFrameHeader → storeFrameHeader (×7) → init → getBlockHeader → storeBlockHeader (×4) → getCBlock → storeCBlock (×cBlockSize) → decode-into-dst → getBlockHeader → … → getSuffix`. Assert the returned `nextSrcSizeHint` after **every** call and the cumulative output. | [ ] |\n| 80 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **1 byte of src AND 1 byte of dst per call**. Fixture #25 (blockLinked, contentChecksum on, 4 blocks). Adds `dstage_flushOut` partial flushing (`tmpOutStart` advancing 1 byte at a time), `LZ4F_updateDict(..., withinTmp=1)`, the post-loop history-preservation branch, and `dstage_storeSuffix` for the trailing content CRC. | [ ] |\n| 81 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **3-byte src chunks** (never a multiple of `BHSize == 4`), dst = 4096 bytes. Fixture #26 (blockChecksum on, blockLinked, 4 blocks). Guarantees `dstage_storeBlockHeader` and `dstage_storeCBlock` on every block, plus a block CRC that always straddles a chunk boundary. | [ ] |\n| 82 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **Hint-driven loop**: `*srcSizePtr` for each call = the `nextSrcSizeHint` returned by the previous call (starting at `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX`), dst = `maxBlockSize`. Fixtures #17 (256 KB linked), #20 (1 MB independent), #26 (blockChecksum), #25 (contentChecksum). This is the \"well-behaved caller\" path where `getBlockHeader`/`getCBlock` always have enough input and `storeCBlock` is never entered. | [ ] |\n| 83 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **dst smaller than `maxBlockSize`, `blockIndependent`**: fixture #16 (`max64KB`, `blockIndependent`, 4 blocks + tail). `*dstSizePtr = 1000` per call, src = whole frame at once. Forces the `decode into tmpOut` branch + `dstage_flushOut` for every block; `blockMode != blockLinked` ⇒ no `LZ4F_updateDict`, no post-loop history preservation. | [ ] |\n| 84 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **dst smaller than `maxBlockSize`, `blockLinked`**: fixture #15. `*dstSizePtr = 1000` per call, src = whole frame at once, `dOptPtr = NULL` (`stableDst = 0`). Exercises `tmpOut` decode + `flushOut` + `LZ4F_updateDict(withinTmp=1)` + the post-loop `dstage_flushOut` history-preservation branch (`preserveSize`/`copySize`/`oldDictEnd` arithmetic). Repeat with `*dstSizePtr = 1` and `= 65535`. | [ ] |\n| 85 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **dst capacity exactly at the