l frame; (c) two real frames back to back with different `blockSizeID`s (#12 then #21). Feed one-shot and 1-byte-at-a-time. `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` is called internally at each frame end, so the next frame must decode without any caller action; assert `LZ4F_decompress` returns `0` exactly at each frame boundary and stops consuming there when given the whole buffer. | [ ] |\n| 99 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **`dstage_init` buffer allocation across `maxBlockSize`.** Decode the #13/#17/#19/#21 fixtures (blockSizeID 4/5/6/7) each with `*dstSizePtr` = that blockSize, on a **fresh** dctx (`bufferNeeded = maxBlockSize + (linked?128KB:0) > maxBufferSize` ⇒ allocate `tmpIn = maxBlockSize + 4` and `tmpOutBuffer = bufferNeeded`). Then, on **one reused** dctx, decode #21 (4 MB) first and #13 (64 KB) second ⇒ `bufferNeeded <= maxBufferSize` ⇒ no reallocation; and the reverse order ⇒ reallocation. Also mix `blockLinked` (+128 KB) and `blockIndependent` (+0) fixtures on the same dctx. | [ ] |\n| 100 | `LZ4F_decompress` | **Frame-boundary edge shapes.** (a) Fixture #9 (empty frame: 7-byte header + 4-byte endMark) — `dstBuffer` non-NULL with `*dstSizePtr = 0`, and `dstBuffer = NULL` with `*dstSizePtr = 0`; `blockHeader == 0` ⇒ straight to `dstage_getSuffix`. (b) A src buffer holding the #15 frame **plus 100 trailing 0xFF bytes**: `LZ4F_decompress` must stop exactly at the end of the frame, report `*srcSizePtr` == frame length, and return `0`. (c) The #15 frame with `*dstSizePtr` exactly one byte larger than the content. | [ ] |\n\n## lz4frame.c — dictionary / CDict\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 101 | `LZ4F_createCDict`, `LZ4F_freeCDict` | `dictBuffer` non-NULL with `dictSize = 0` ⇒ 0-byte `dictContent` allocation, `LZ4_loadDictSlow`/`LZ4_loadDictHC` with size 0. Then `LZ4F_freeCDict(cdict)`; also `LZ4F_freeCDict(NULL)`. Use the resulting CDict in `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` with `src = TEXT(1000)` and assert the output equals the `cdict = NULL` output. | [ ] |\n| 102 | `LZ4F_createCDict`, `LZ4F_freeCDict`, `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | `dictSize = 1024` (`dict = TEXT(1024)`) and `dictSize = 65536` (exactly 64 KB, `dict = TEXT(65536)`) — the `dictSize > 64 KB` truncation branch is **not** taken. `cctx` from `LZ4F_createCompressionContext`; prefs = INIT + `dictID = 0xABCD1234` + `level = 0`; `src = TEXT(1000)`. Round-trip via `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` with the same dict. | [ ] |\n| 103 | `LZ4F_createCDict`, `LZ4F_freeCDict`, `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | `dictSize = 200000` (> 64 KB) ⇒ `dictStart += dictSize - 65536; dictSize = 65536` (only the **last** 64 KB are kept). Assert the compressed output is byte-identical to `LZ4F_createCDict(dict + 200000 - 65536, 65536)`. Also `dictSize = 65537` (one byte over the boundary). prefs = INIT + `level = 9`; `src = TEXT(5000)`. | [ ] |\n| 104 | `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced`, `LZ4F_freeCDict`, `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | `customMem = LZ4F_defaultCMem` (all fields NULL ⇒ `LZ4F_malloc` falls through to `malloc`), `dictSize = 65536`. Assert the CDict behaves identically to `LZ4F_createCDict` on the same dict (compare the frames produced with prefs = INIT + `level = 0` and `level = 9`, `src = TEXT(3000)`). | [ ] |\n| 105 | `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | `cdict = NULL`, `preferencesPtr = NULL`, `src` ∈ {`RUN(1)`, `TEXT(65536)`, `TEXT(300000)`, `RAND(64)`}; `cctx` from `LZ4F_createCompressionContext`. Output must be byte-identical to `LZ4F_compressFrame` for the same src (this is exactly what `LZ4F_compressFrame` delegates to, minus the stack-context optimisation). | [ ] |\n| 106 | `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | CDict from `TEXT(65536)`; prefs = INIT + `compressionLevel = 1` (`< LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` ⇒ `LZ4F_compressBlock` with `cdict != NULL` ⇒ `LZ4_resetStream_fast` + `LZ4_attach_dictionary` + `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`), `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`; `src = TEXT(1000)` (single block; `srcSize <= blockSize` ⇒ `blockMode` forced to `blockIndependent`). | [ ] |\n| 107 | `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | Same CDict; prefs = INIT + `compressionLevel = 9` (`>= LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` ⇒ `LZ4F_compressBlockHC` with `cdict != NULL` ⇒ `LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast` + `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary` + `LZ4_compress_HC_continue`); `src = TEXT(1000)`. Also `compressionLevel = 12` + `favorDecSpeed = 1`, and `compressionLevel = -3`. | [ ] |\n| 108 | `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | Same CDict; prefs = INIT + `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `blockMode = LZ4F_blockLinked`, `level = 0`; `src = TEXT(300000)` (> blockSize ⇒ `blockMode` stays `blockLinked` ⇒ `LZ4F_initStream` runs **once** at `compressBegin` and blocks use `LZ4F_compressBlock_continue`, which ignores `cdict`). Only the first block benefits from the dict. | [ ] |\n| 109 | `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` | Same CDict; prefs = INIT + `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB`, `blockMode = LZ4F_blockIndependent` explicitly, `level = 0`; `src = TEXT(300000)` (4 blocks + tail) ⇒ `LZ4F_compressBlock` re-attaches the dictionary for **every** block. Repeat with `level = 9` (`LZ4F_compressBlockHC` per block) and with `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max4MB` (⇒ `LZ4F_optimalBSID` downgrades to 6). | [ ] |\n| 110 | `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_flush`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | CDict from `TEXT(65536)`; prefs = INIT + `dictID = 0x5A5A5A5A` + `compressionLevel = 2` + `blockMode = LZ4F_blockIndependent` + `blockSizeID = LZ4F_max64KB` + `autoFlush = 0` + `contentChecksumFlag = enabled`; `dstCapacity = 19` for begin. Then 30 × 5000-byte `compressUpdate` calls over `TEXT(150000)` with `cOptPtr = NULL`, a `LZ4F_flush` after update 10, and `compressEnd`. Note `blockMode` is **not** downgraded here (no `LZ4F_optimalBSID` / no forced independence on the low-level path). Round-trip via `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`. | [ ] |\n| 111 | `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict`, `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_compressEnd` | `dict = TEXT(1024)`, `dictSize