(never block-aligned). Assert both files decode via the file API and via plain `LZ4F_decompress`. | [ ] |\n| 125 | `LZ4F_readOpen`, `LZ4F_read`, `LZ4F_readClose` | **Read side over externally produced frames.** Write the #22 (`max4MB`, `blockIndependent`, `MIX(16777216)`), #25 (`contentChecksum`), #27 (`blockChecksum` + stored blocks) and #30 (19-byte header, `contentSize` + `dictID`, `max4MB`) fixtures to disk with plain `fwrite` (not `LZ4F_writeOpen`), then read each back with `LZ4F_readOpen`/`LZ4F_read`/`LZ4F_readClose`. Read chunk sizes: 1, 4096, `blockSize`, `blockSize + 1`, and the whole content. Assert `readOpen`'s `blockSizeID` switch selects the right `srcBufMaxSize` for each ID (64 KB / 256 KB / 1 MB / 4 MB) and that `srcBufSize = 19 - consumedSize` correctly carries over the leftover header bytes (7-byte header ⇒ 12 bytes carried, 19-byte header ⇒ 0 carried). Also call `LZ4F_read` again after EOF ⇒ must return 0. | [ ] |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1953,"cache_read_input_tokens":104036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1953,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012ozyaAj364xJsN3PMvqK91","session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"eb69bb30-1935-4a1f-a3f2-7b79a4d3dc1a","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:17:10.247Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"CONFIGS table for lz4frame/lz4file"}
