{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pxb5bqphazsnsubvnmkaajajvwqkyswfti34ttkxzb2r3cbdulwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016UzAKZwKyMNJCsJYRtsyw8","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Write lz4frame decompression tests","prompt":"Write Rust differential integration tests for the DECOMPRESSION side of lz4frame.c, plus all of lz4file.c, in an LZ4 C-to-Rust translation.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\n## Context\n- `c_src/src/lz4frame.c`, `c_src/src/lz4file.c` + headers `c_src/include/lz4frame.h`,\n  `c_src/include/lz4frame_static.h`, `c_src/include/lz4file.h` are the C ground truth.\n  `src/lz4frame.rs` and `src/lz4file.rs` are the Rust translations.\n- The C is ALWAYS correct. If outputs diverge, FIX THE RUST, never the C.\n  DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`.\n- Already built: C = `c_src/build/liblz4.so`, Rust = `target/release/liblz4.so`.\n\n## MANDATORY: use the existing harness\nREAD `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST, and read `tests/lz4_stream.rs` as a worked example of\nthe required style. It provides:\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way to obtain functions.\n  NEVER call Rust code directly, never `use lz4::...`. All calls go through the `.so`\n  export tables via libloading so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are tested too.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`: `next_u64`, `next_u32`, `byte`, `below(n)`, `range(lo,hi)`, `bool()`\n- `gen_shape(&mut rng, shape, len)`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name(shape)`\n- `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c_bytes, rust_bytes)`\n- `#[repr(C)]` types `LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, `LZ4F_preferences_t` (with `Default` impls\n  mirroring `LZ4F_INIT_FRAMEINFO`/`LZ4F_INIT_PREFERENCES`), `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`,\n  `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_CustomMem`\n- All the `LZ4F_*` constants, `lz4f_is_error(code)`, `lz4f_error_code(code)`, and the\n  `err::` module with every numeric `LZ4F_ERROR_*` value.\n- **HARNESS RULE**: pre-fill the C dst buffer and the Rust dst buffer with the SAME\n  sentinel byte (`0xAA`), then compare the FULL buffer. Different fills give false\n  positives on untouched bytes.\n\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\n`size_t` == `usize`; `LZ4F_dctx*` is opaque -> `*mut c_void`.\n\n## Entry points you own — cover ALL of them\n\n**lz4frame decompression:**\n- `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext(&dctx, version)` / `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext(dctx)`\n- `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced(customMem, version)` with\n  `LZ4F_CustomMem::default()`\n- `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext(dctx)`\n- `LZ4F_headerSize(src, srcSize)` — on real headers of EVERY option combination (the\n  header length varies with contentSize/dictID presence), on truncated headers of every\n  length 0..19, and on skippable-frame magics\n- `LZ4F_getFrameInfo(dctx, &frameInfo, src, &srcSize)` — called BEFORE any decompress,\n  and again MID-STREAM after partial decompression; compare the returned code, the\n  mutated `srcSize` out-param, AND every field of the returned `LZ4F_frameInfo_t`\n- `LZ4F_decompress(dctx, dst, &dstSize, src, &srcSize, dOptPtr)` — compare the return\n  value (the \"hint\"), both mutated out-params, and the output bytes\n- `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict(dctx, dst, &dstSize, src, &srcSize, dict, dictSize, dOptPtr)`\n- `LZ4F_getBlockSize(blockSizeID)`\nVerify every signature against the C source before using it.\n\n**lz4file.c (all 6 exported symbols):**\n- `LZ4F_writeOpen(&state, FILE*, prefsPtr)`, `LZ4F_write(state, buf, size)`,\n  `LZ4F_writeClose(state)`\n- `LZ4F_readOpen(&state, FILE*)`, `LZ4F_read(state, buf, size)`, `LZ4F_readClose(state)`\nUse real temp files. Get `FILE*` via libc `fopen`/`fclose`/`fflush`/`rewind` — declare\nthem yourself with `extern \"C\"` (that is fine; they are libc, not the library under\ntest). Put temp files under the directory from the `TMPDIR` env var, with distinct names\nper test, and clean them up.\n\n## Axes to sweep\n\n**Frame option axes (these change what the decoder must parse):**\n- `blockSizeID` 0,4,5,6,7 ; `blockMode` linked/independent ;\n  `contentChecksumFlag` 0/1 ; `blockChecksumFlag` 0/1 ;\n  `contentSize` 0 vs exact size ; `dictID` 0 vs non-zero ;\n  `frameType` LZ4F_frame vs LZ4F_skippableFrame ;\n  `compressionLevel` spanning the LZ4-fast regime and all three LZ4HC regimes\n  (levels 1-2 `lz4mid`, 3-9 hashChain, 10-12 optimal) ; `autoFlush` 0/1\n\n**Decompress-side option axes:**\n- `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t.stableDst` 0 and 1\n- `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t.skipChecksums` 0 and 1\n- NULL `dOptPtr`\n\n**Call-pattern axes — THE most important thing here.** `LZ4F_decompress` is a state\nmachine (`dStage`); to drive it through every state you must feed input in many\ndifferent granularities:\n- the whole frame in ONE call\n- ONE BYTE AT A TIME (this is what forces `storeFrameHeader`, `storeBlockHeader`,\n  `storeCBlock`, `storeSuffix`, `storeSFrameSize`)\n- fixed src chunk sizes 1,2,3,4,5,7,16,64,1000\n- RANDOM src chunk sizes (seeded)\n- and independently, DST capacity granularity: a dst buffer smaller than the block\n  size (forces the `tmpOut` path and partial `flushOut`), dst exactly one byte, and a\n  dst large enough for everything\n- the full cross-product of a few src-chunk sizes x a few dst-capacity sizes\nRead the `dStage` enum in lz4frame.c and add a comment listing which of your test\nconfigurations reaches each state; aim to reach ALL of them.\n\n**Content axes:** all `N_SHAPES` shapes; sizes 0,1,2,blockSize-1,blockSize,blockSize+1,\nseveral blocks, many blocks. Random data produces stored/uncompressed blocks; repetitive\ndata produces long matches.\n\n**Dictionary axes:** compress with `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` /\n`LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict`, then decode with `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`; dict sizes\n0, 1, 100, 4096, 65535, 65536, 70000.\n\n**Skippable frames:** decode a lone skippable frame; a skippable frame FOLLOWED by a real\nframe in the same buffer; skippable magics across the whole valid range\n0x184D2A50..=0x184D2A5F.\n\n**Multi-frame:** two concatenated real frames decoded with the same dctx (with\n`LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` between, and without).\n\n## What to assert\nFor every configuration: call BOTH libraries and assert\n1. identical return value from EVERY call (including the streaming \"hint\" values),\n2. identical mutated out-params (`dstSizePtr`, `srcSizePtr`) at every step,\n3. byte-identical output buffers (full buffer, same sentinel prefill),\n4. the decoded content equals the original input.\n\n## Deliverable\nWrite TWO files: `tests/lz4frame_decompress_diff.rs` and `tests/lz4file_diff.rs`.\n\nThen make BOTH pass:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4frame_decompress_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4file_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nAlways use `--release --offline`. Other agents may be building concurrently, so if cargo\nblocks on the target lock, just wait / retry. After ANY edit to `src/*.rs`, run\n`timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running (the tests load the\nbuilt `.so`).\n\nKeep each file's runtime under ~180 seconds; byte-at-a-time decoding of a 4 MB frame is\nvery slow, so use SMALL inputs for the fine-grained chunking rows and large inputs only\nfor the coarse rows.\n\nReport back: exact `#[test]` function names per file, the final pass/fail lines, every\ndivergence found with the precise C-vs-Rust difference and how you fixed the Rust, and\nwhich `dStage` states you believe you covered."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":569,"cache_read_input_tokens":155190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":569,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"a44d4d1f-b8ca-4bfa-b1f6-2bf59ec4bab3","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:17:44.632Z"}
