stinct way the C code rejects or errors on input, derived **mechanically**\nfrom the C source (every `RETURN_ERROR` / `RETURN_ERROR_IF`, every `return 0` /\n`return -1` / `return NULL` failure sentinel, every `assert`, every explicit range\ncheck, null check, and min/max constant). One row per distinct rejection branch —\nthree distinct `RETURN_ERROR` branches are three rows.\n\n**{total} rows total**, numbered globally and sequentially:\n\n| C source file | rows | count |\n|---------------|------|-------|\n| `lz4.c`      | 1–{n1} | {n1} |\n| `lz4hc.c`    | {n1+1}–{n1+n2} | {n2} |\n| `xxhash.c`   | {n1+n2+1}–{n1+n2+n3} | {n3} |\n| `lz4frame.c` | {n1+n2+n3+1}–{n1+n2+n3+n_frame} | {n_frame} |\n| `lz4file.c`  | {n1+n2+n3+n_frame+1}–{total} | {n_file} |\n| **total**    |      | **{total}** |\n\n## Phase C status\n\nEach section below is followed by the differential test file that covers it.\nA row is \"covered\" when a test constructs that exact invalid input/condition,\ncalls BOTH the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`, and asserts they return the SAME\nerror code / sentinel.\n\n| C source file | test file | result |\n|---------------|-----------|--------|\n| `lz4.c`      | `tests/lz4_errors.rs`            | see test run |\n| `lz4hc.c`    | `tests/lz4hc_diff.rs`            | see test run |\n| `xxhash.c`   | `tests/xxhash_diff.rs`           | see test run |\n| `lz4frame.c` | `tests/lz4frame_errors.rs`       | see test run |\n| `lz4file.c`  | `tests/lz4file_diff.rs`          | see test run |\n\nRows that are intentionally NOT exercised (compile-time `#error` guards,\nun-forceable `malloc` failures, and rows the C itself documents as\n`assert`-only/undefined behaviour, which would fault both libraries identically\nand prove nothing) are listed with their reason at the end of the corresponding\ntest file.\n\n\"\"\"\n\nout = [hdr] + s_lz4 + [''] + s_hc + [''] + s_xxh + [''] + s_frame + [''] + s_file + [''] + s_enum + [''] + s_notes\nopen('ERRORS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(out))\npri