ctually branches on —\nevery runtime option/mode/flag the public API can set, every input SHAPE the code\nspecial-cases, and the FULL set of public entry points **including the lowest-level\nones**, not just the convenience / one-shot wrappers.\n\nRows are the cross-product of those axes, pruned to the combinations the C actually\ndistinguishes. Each row is driven with MANY randomized inputs (fixed seed, so runs are\nreproducible), not a single hand-picked value.\n\n**{tot} rows total**, numbered globally and sequentially:\n\n| section | rows | count | covering test file |\n|---------|------|-------|--------------------|\n| `lz4.c` — block API              | {b[0]}–{b[1]-1} | {n[0]} | `tests/lz4_block.rs`, `tests/lz4_stream.rs` |\n| `lz4hc.c` — HC API               | {b[1]}–{b[2]-1} | {n[1]} | `tests/lz4hc_diff.rs` |\n| `xxhash.c`                       | {b[2]}–{b[3]-1} | {n[2]} | `tests/xxhash_diff.rs` |\n| `lz4frame.c` — compression       | {b[3]}–{b[4]-1} | {n[3]} | `tests/lz4frame_compress_diff.rs` |\n| `lz4frame.c` — decompression     | {b[4]}–{b[5]-1} | {n[4]} | `tests/lz4frame_decompress_diff.rs` |\n| `lz4frame.c` — dictionary/CDict  | {b[5]}–{b[6]-1} | {n[5]} | `tests/lz4frame_compress_diff.rs` |\n| `lz4file.c`                      | {b[6]}–{b[7]-1} | {n[6]} | `tests/lz4file_diff.rs` |\n| **total**                        |      | **{tot}** | |\n\nA row's `[ ]` becomes `[x]` only once its configuration passes byte-for-byte\nagreement between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` across the randomized inputs.\n\n\"\"\"\n\nout = ([hdr] + p1_pre + s_lz4 + [''] + s_hc + [''] + s_xxh + ['']\n       + p2_pre + s_fcomp + [''] + s_fdecomp + [''] + s_fdict + [''] + s_file)\nopen('CONFIGS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(out))\nprint(\"wrote CONFIGS.md; counts:\", n, \"total\", tot)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/build_configs.py\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nrows=[int(m.group(1)) for m in (re.match(r'^\\|\\s*(\\d+)\\s*\\|',l) for l in open('CONFIGS.md')) if m]\nprint(\"rows:\",len(rows),