{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_i6hchhiuknmyadysqwpkyvw6w5njjh7jbxthnlnsyizasubaxxqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01S2PEEpiVj3PSNFgiirvFeF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> CONFIGS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Build-time configuration surface (Phase A step 1 / Phase D)\n\nEnumerated mechanically from `Cargo.toml` and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`.\n\n### Rust side — `Cargo.toml`\n\n```toml\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n# NO [features] section is declared, and no `default = [...]` key.\n```\n\nThere is therefore exactly **ONE** valid feature combination: the empty set.\n`./check_all_features.sh check` enumerates the power set of the declared\nfeatures (which is `{ {} }`) and runs\n`cargo check --release --offline --all-targets --no-default-features --features ''`\nfor it; `./check_all_features.sh test` runs the whole differential suite for it.\nAny future `[features]` entry is picked up automatically — the script derives the\npower set from `Cargo.toml`, it does not hard-code the list.\n\n### C side — `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`\n\nThe C library is compiled with a single fixed configuration; there are no\n`option()`s or alternative targets, so there is no C-side combinatorial axis to\nmirror:\n\n| define | value | effect on the code under test |\n|--------|-------|-------------------------------|\n| `XXH_NAMESPACE` | `LZ4_` | prefixes every exported xxhash symbol, hence `LZ4_XXH32`, `LZ4_XXH64`, … |\n| `LZ4_HEAPMODE`  | `0`    | `LZ4_compress_fast` / `LZ4_compress_destSize` put the hash table on the **stack**; the `ALLOC` failure branches (`ERRORS.md` rows 21, 22) are not compiled in |\n| `LZ4F_HEAPMODE` | `0`    | `LZ4F_compressFrame` uses a stack-allocated cctx |\n| `CMAKE_C_STANDARD` | `99` | — |\n\nBecause `LZ4_HEAPMODE=0` / `LZ4F_HEAPMODE=0`, the heap-allocation-failure error\nrows are **absent from the binary under test**, which is why they are listed as\ndeliberately-not-tested in `tests/lz4_errors.rs` rather than left unchecked.\n\n### Consequence for Phase D\n\n\"Repeat Phases B–C for EVERY feature combination\" resolves to the single default\nconfiguration, and the whole suite is run against it. There is no second code\npath to switch to, and no `#[cfg(feature = \"...\")]` gating is required anywhere\nin `src/` (verified: `grep -rn 'cfg(feature' src/` returns nothing).\nEOF\ngrep -rn 'cfg(feature' src/ | head; echo \"cfg(feature) occurrences in src/: $(grep -rn 'cfg(feature' src/ | wc -l)\"","description":"Document build config surface and verify no cfg(feature) usage"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":866,"cache_read_input_tokens":232726,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":866,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"158259da-af4a-4e12-b7bf-4ea374f53ceb","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:25:31.576Z"}
