{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BFVP8uBwDpE2vBQE9jRXjX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: aa9cba9b2b9e415d1 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'aa9cba9b2b9e415d1', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ieCE1Y-translated-rust/5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b/tasks/aa9cba9b2b9e415d1.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"d1473a12-2057-42e7-a264-fb9d1b8b86d0","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:29:28.387Z","tool_use_result":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"aa9cba9b2b9e415d1","description":"lz4frame one-shot + metadata tests","resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","prompt":"Write Rust differential integration tests for the ONE-SHOT + METADATA parts of lz4frame.c in an LZ4 C-to-Rust translation.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\nKeep your scope TIGHT: only the symbols listed below. Another agent owns the streaming\ncompression API and another owns decompression — do NOT write tests for those, and do NOT\ncreate or edit any file other than the ONE file named below (plus `src/lz4frame.rs` if you\nfind a real divergence).\n\n## Context\n- `c_src/src/lz4frame.c` + `c_src/include/lz4frame.h` + `c_src/include/lz4frame_static.h`\n  are the C ground truth. `src/lz4frame.rs` is the Rust translation.\n- The C is ALWAYS correct. On divergence FIX THE RUST, never the C.\n  DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`.\n- Already built: C = `c_src/build/liblz4.so`, Rust = `target/release/liblz4.so`.\n\n## MANDATORY harness\nREAD `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST and `tests/lz4_errors.rs` as a style example. It provides:\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way to obtain functions. NEVER\n  call Rust code directly, never `use lz4::...`. All calls go through the `.so` export\n  tables via libloading, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are tested too.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`: `next_u64`, `next_u32`, `byte`, `below(n)`, `range(lo,hi)`, `bool()`\n- `gen_shape(&mut rng, shape, len)`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name(shape)`\n- `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c_bytes, rust_bytes)`\n- `#[repr(C)]` `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` / `LZ4F_preferences_t` (with `Default` impls mirroring\n  `LZ4F_INIT_FRAMEINFO` / `LZ4F_INIT_PREFERENCES`), `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`,\n  `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_CustomMem`\n- All `LZ4F_*` constants, `lz4f_is_error(code)`, `lz4f_error_code(code)`, and `err::*`\n  with every numeric `LZ4F_ERROR_*` value (e.g. `err::ERROR_maxBlockSize_invalid == 2`).\n- **HARNESS RULE**: pre-fill the C dst buffer and the Rust dst buffer with the SAME\n  sentinel byte (`0xAA`), then compare the FULL buffer. Different fills give false\n  positives on untouched bytes. (Real mistake already made and fixed once — don't repeat it.)\n- IMPORTANT: write hex seeds carefully — `0xF1LL` etc. are invalid Rust literals. Use only\n  0-9a-fA-F digits and `_`.\n\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\n`size_t` == `usize`; `LZ4F_cctx*` / `LZ4F_CDict*` are opaque -> `*mut c_void`.\n\n## YOUR SYMBOLS (only these)\n`LZ4F_getVersion`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`, `LZ4F_getBlockSize`, `LZ4F_isError`,\n`LZ4F_getErrorName`, `LZ4F_getErrorCode`, `LZ4F_compressFrameBound`, `LZ4F_compressBound`,\n`LZ4F_compressFrame`, `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict`, `LZ4F_createCDict`,\n`LZ4F_createCDict_advanced`, `LZ4F_freeCDict`, `LZ4F_headerSize`.\nVerify EVERY signature against the C source before using it.\n\n## What to cover\n\n**Metadata / trivial:** `LZ4F_getVersion()`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max()`.\n\n**`LZ4F_getBlockSize`** for EVERY int value in -8..=16 plus `i32::MIN`, `i32::MAX`,\n`0x7FFFFFFF`, and randomized ints. This is a C enum parameter, so out-of-range values are\nreal inputs. Assert identical `size_t` return, and that invalid IDs give\n`LZ4F_ERROR_maxBlockSize_invalid` (code 2) in BOTH (ERRORS.md rows 168/169).\n\n**`LZ4F_isError` / `LZ4F_getErrorCode`** for: 0, 1, 100, every `-(size_t)code` for\ncode 0..=24, `-(size_t)25`, `-(size_t)100`, `usize::MAX`, `usize::MAX/2`, and randomized\n`usize` values. Assert identical returns.\n\n**`LZ4F_getErrorName`** for every code 0..=24 AND several out-of-range codes: compare the\nreturned C string BYTES (use `CStr::from_ptr(...).to_bytes()`), not the pointers.\n\n**`LZ4F_compressFrameBound` and `LZ4F_compressBound`**: with `NULL` prefs, and with the\ncross-product of `blockSizeID` {0,4,5,6,7}, `blockMode` {linked,independent},\n`contentChecksumFlag` {0,1}, `blockChecksumFlag` {0,1}, `autoFlush` {0,1},\n`contentSize` {0, srcSize}, `dictID` {0, 0xDEADBEEF},\n`compressionLevel` {i32::MIN,-1,0,1,2,3,9,10,12,13,i32::MAX}.\nsrcSize sweep: 0,1,2,15,16,65535,65536,65537,262144,1048576,4194304,4194305, and randomized.\nAssert identical `size_t` returns.\n\n**`LZ4F_compressFrame`** — the main event. For the SAME preference cross-product as above\n(prune sensibly to keep runtime reasonable, but cover every axis value at least once and\nevery blockSizeID x blockMode x both checksum flags combination):\n- srcSize: 0, 1, 2, 15, blockSize-1, blockSize, blockSize+1, 2*blockSize+7, several\n  blocks, plus randomized sizes. Derive blockSize from `LZ4F_getBlockSize(blockSizeID)`.\n- all `N_SHAPES` data shapes (random data forces the \"stored/uncompressed block\" path\n  where the block header's high bit is set; repetitive data forces long matches).\n- `compressionLevel` spanning EVERY regime: negative (LZ4 fast/acceleration), 0, 1\n  (**note `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN == 2` in this tree, so level 1 is LZ4-fast and level 2 is\n  already LZ4HC**), 2 (LZ4HC `lz4mid`), 3..9 (LZ4HC hashChain), 10..12 (LZ4HC optimal),\n  and >12 (clamped).\n- `frameType` LZ4F_frame and LZ4F_skippableFrame.\n- dstCapacity exactly `LZ4F_compressFrameBound(...)`, and larger.\nAssert: identical return value AND byte-identical full dst buffer. Then round-trip the\nC-produced frame through `LZ4F_decompress` (obtained from BOTH libs) and assert it yields\nthe original bytes.\n\n**CDict path:** `LZ4F_createCDict(dict, dictSize)` and\n`LZ4F_createCDict_advanced(LZ4F_CustomMem::default(), dict, dictSize)` for dict sizes\n0, 1, 8, 100, 4096, 65535, 65536, 70000 (>64 KB is truncated to the last 64 KB inside);\nassert both return non-NULL identically. Then `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict(cctx, dst,\ndstCapacity, src, srcSize, cdict, prefs)` across the same preference axes and assert\nbyte-identical output. Finally `LZ4F_freeCDict` (and `LZ4F_freeCDict(NULL)`, which the C\naccepts — ERRORS.md says free-on-NULL is fine).\nNOTE: `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict`'s first parameter is an `LZ4F_cctx*`; check the C\nsource for whether NULL is allowed and mirror exactly what it does.\n\n**`LZ4F_headerSize`:** on the first bytes of real frames produced with EVERY option\ncombination (the header length varies with contentSize/dictID presence), on truncated\nheaders of every length 0..=19, on all 16 skippable magics\n0x184D2A50..=0x184D2A5F, and on garbage/random buffers. Assert identical `size_t` returns\nincluding the error cases (`frameHeader_incomplete` = 12, `frameType_unknown` = 13).\n\n**Error rows you own** (assert the SAME error code via `lz4f_error_code`, not just \"failed\"):\n- rows 168/169: `LZ4F_getBlockSize` invalid ID -> `maxBlockSize_invalid` (2)\n- row 170: `LZ4F_compressFrame` / `_usingCDict` with `dstCapacity <\n  LZ4F_compressFrameBound(...)` -> `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` (11). Sweep dstCapacity from 0\n  up to just below the bound, for several preference sets.\n- rows 179/180: `LZ4F_createCDict*` allocation failure -> returns NULL. **This IS testable**\n  via `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` with a `LZ4F_CustomMem` whose `customAlloc`/`customCalloc`\n  returns NULL (or returns NULL only after the Nth call, so you can fail each of the four\n  sub-allocations independently). Write `extern \"C\"` allocator callbacks with a\n  thread-local/static counter. Assert BOTH libraries return NULL.\n- Also cover generic boundaries: NULL `prefsPtr` (documented as valid = defaults), NULL\n  src with srcSize 0, and out-of-range enum values for `blockSizeID` / `blockMode` /\n  `contentChecksumFlag` / `blockChecksumFlag` / `frameType` passed across the FFI (C enums\n  accept any int; per ERRORS.md the compress side masks these with `& 1` and does NOT\n  validate them, so assert the C and Rust agree on the resulting frame bytes).\n\n## Deliverable\nWrite ONE file: `tests/lz4frame_oneshot_diff.rs`.\n\nMake it PASS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4frame_oneshot_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nAlways `--release --offline`. Other agents build concurrently — if cargo blocks on the\ntarget lock, wait and retry. After ANY edit to `src/lz4frame.rs`, run\n`timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running.\nKeep runtime under ~150 s: 4 MB block sizes and HC level 12 are slow, so use big block\nsizes only with small inputs and scale iteration counts, while KEEPING every axis covered.\n\nReport back: exact `#[test]` names, the final pass/fail line, every divergence found with\nthe precise C-vs-Rust difference and the fix you made to the Rust, and confirm which of\nyour 14 symbols you exercised.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ieCE1Y-translated-rust/5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b/tasks/aa9cba9b2b9e415d1.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
