{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a83afac96ffa104c1","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Gpbpa8ngqit8KQEP7NNJvK","description":"lz4frame streaming compression tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Write Rust differential integration tests for the STREAMING COMPRESSION API of lz4frame.c in an LZ4 C-to-Rust translation.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\nKeep your scope TIGHT: only the symbols listed below. Another agent owns the one-shot\n`LZ4F_compressFrame` / bounds / `LZ4F_headerSize` / CDict-creation surface, and another owns\ndecompression — do NOT write tests for those, and do NOT create or edit any file other than\nthe ONE file named below (plus `src/lz4frame.rs` if you find a real divergence).\n\n## Context\n- `c_src/src/lz4frame.c` + `c_src/include/lz4frame.h` + `c_src/include/lz4frame_static.h`\n  are the C ground truth. `src/lz4frame.rs` is the Rust translation.\n- The C is ALWAYS correct. On divergence FIX THE RUST, never the C.\n  DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`.\n- Already built: C = `c_src/build/liblz4.so`, Rust = `target/release/liblz4.so`.\n\n## MANDATORY harness\nREAD `tests/common/mod.rs` FIRST and `tests/lz4_stream.rs` as a style example. It provides:\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way to obtain functions. NEVER\n  call Rust code directly, never `use lz4::...`. All calls go through the `.so` export\n  tables via libloading, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are tested too.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`: `next_u64`, `next_u32`, `byte`, `below(n)`, `range(lo,hi)`, `bool()`\n- `gen_shape(&mut rng, shape, len)`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name(shape)`\n- `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c_bytes, rust_bytes)`\n- `#[repr(C)]` `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` / `LZ4F_preferences_t` (with `Default` impls mirroring\n  `LZ4F_INIT_FRAMEINFO` / `LZ4F_INIT_PREFERENCES`), `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`,\n  `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_CustomMem`\n- All `LZ4F_*` constants, `lz4f_is_error(code)`, `lz4f_error_code(code)`, and `err::*` with\n  every numeric `LZ4F_ERROR_*` value (e.g. `err::ERROR_compressionState_uninitialized == 20`,\n  `err::ERROR_dstMaxSize_tooSmall == 11`, `err::ERROR_parameter_null == 21`,\n  `err::ERROR_allocation_failed == 9`, `err::ERROR_parameter_invalid == 4`).\n- **HARNESS RULE**: pre-fill the C dst buffer and the Rust dst buffer with the SAME\n  sentinel byte (`0xAA`), then compare the FULL buffer. Different fills give false\n  positives on untouched bytes. (Real mistake already made and fixed once — don't repeat it.)\n- IMPORTANT: write hex seeds carefully — `0xF1LL` etc. are invalid Rust literals. Use only\n  0-9a-fA-F digits and `_`.\n\nStart with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\n```\n`size_t` == `usize`; `LZ4F_cctx*` / `LZ4F_CDict*` are opaque -> `*mut c_void`.\n\n## YOUR SYMBOLS (only these)\n`LZ4F_createCompressionContext`, `LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced`,\n`LZ4F_freeCompressionContext`, `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `LZ4F_compressBegin_internal`,\n`LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict`, `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict`,\n`LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce`, `LZ4F_compressUpdate`, `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate`,\n`LZ4F_flush`, `LZ4F_compressEnd`.\n(You may CALL `LZ4F_compressBound`, `LZ4F_createCDict`, `LZ4F_freeCDict` and\n`LZ4F_decompress` as helpers for sizing and round-trip validation — just don't write\ndedicated tests for them.)\nVerify EVERY signature against the C source before using it. `LZ4F_compressBegin_internal`\nand `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce` are declared in the static/internal header — read\ntheir exact prototypes out of `lz4frame.c` / `lz4frame_static.h`.\n\n## What to cover — drive the API the way a real streaming consumer does\n\n**The full pipeline**, end to end, for each configuration:\n`createCompressionContext` -> `compressBegin*` -> N x (`compressUpdate` /\n`uncompressedUpdate` / `flush`) -> `compressEnd` -> `freeCompressionContext`,\nasserting after EVERY SINGLE CALL that (a) the return values are identical and (b) the\ndestination buffer is byte-identical. Then concatenate the produced output and assert the\nC frame and the Rust frame are byte-identical AND that both round-trip through\n`LZ4F_decompress` back to the original input.\n\n**Preference axes** (cross-product, pruned sensibly, but every value covered at least once\nand every `blockSizeID` x `blockMode` x `blockChecksumFlag` x `contentChecksumFlag`\ncombination present):\n- `blockSizeID` {0,4,5,6,7}; `blockMode` {LZ4F_blockLinked, LZ4F_blockIndependent}\n- `contentChecksumFlag` {0,1}; `blockChecksumFlag` {0,1}\n- `contentSize` {0 (omitted), exact total size (8-byte field written)}\n- `dictID` {0 (omitted), 0xDEADBEEF}\n- `frameType` {LZ4F_frame, LZ4F_skippableFrame}\n- `compressionLevel`: i32::MIN, -65537, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, i32::MAX.\n  **`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN == 2` in this tree**, so the LZ4-fast/LZ4HC switch is between level\n  1 and 2. Level 2 is LZ4HC `lz4mid`, 3-9 hashChain, 10-12 optimal. Cover all regimes.\n- `autoFlush` {0,1}; `favorDecSpeed` {0,1}\n- `LZ4F_compressOptions_t.stableSrc` {0,1}, and a NULL `cOptPtr`\n\n**Chunking axes — the most important thing here.** `LZ4F_compressUpdate` buffers partial\nblocks in `cctx->tmpBuff`/`tmpIn`/`tmpInSize`. Feed the SAME total input via many\ndifferent chunk patterns and assert every intermediate call agrees:\n- one single big chunk\n- one byte at a time\n- fixed chunk sizes 1,2,3,7,16,100,1000,65535\n- chunk sizes landing EXACTLY on the block boundary, and one byte either side\n  (blockSize-1, blockSize, blockSize+1)\n- RANDOM chunk sizes from the seeded Rng\n- zero-length updates interleaved between real updates\n- `LZ4F_flush` called between updates, with `autoFlush=0` AND `autoFlush=1`, including\n  flush when nothing is buffered (must be a no-op returning 0) and flush twice in a row\n\n**`LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate`** (u