de` {LZ4F_blockLinked, LZ4F_blockIndependent}\n- `contentChecksumFlag` {0,1}; `blockChecksumFlag` {0,1}\n- `contentSize` {0 (omitted), exact total size (8-byte field written)}\n- `dictID` {0 (omitted), 0xDEADBEEF}\n- `frameType` {LZ4F_frame, LZ4F_skippableFrame}\n- `compressionLevel`: i32::MIN, -65537, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, i32::MAX.\n  **`LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN == 2` in this tree**, so the LZ4-fast/LZ4HC switch is between level\n  1 and 2. Level 2 is LZ4HC `lz4mid`, 3-9 hashChain, 10-12 optimal. Cover all regimes.\n- `autoFlush` {0,1}; `favorDecSpeed` {0,1}\n- `LZ4F_compressOptions_t.stableSrc` {0,1}, and a NULL `cOptPtr`\n\n**Chunking axes — the most important thing here.** `LZ4F_compressUpdate` buffers partial\nblocks in `cctx->tmpBuff`/`tmpIn`/`tmpInSize`. Feed the SAME total input via many\ndifferent chunk patterns and assert every intermediate call agrees:\n- one single big chunk\n- one byte at a time\n- fixed chunk sizes 1,2,3,7,16,100,1000,65535\n- chunk sizes landing EXACTLY on the block boundary, and one byte either side\n  (blockSize-1, blockSize, blockSize+1)\n- RANDOM chunk sizes from the seeded Rng\n- zero-length updates interleaved between real updates\n- `LZ4F_flush` called between updates, with `autoFlush=0` AND `autoFlush=1`, including\n  flush when nothing is buffered (must be a no-op returning 0) and flush twice in a row\n\n**`LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate`** (uncompressed/stored blocks): only meaningful with\n`LZ4F_blockIndependent`. Test it alone, and MIXED with `LZ4F_compressUpdate` in both\norders so the C's \"flush buffered data first when blockCompressMode changes\" path\n(lz4frame.c:1012-1016) is exercised. Read that code and make sure you hit it.\n\n**Dictionary axes:** `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` and `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDictOnce`\nwith dict sizes 0, 1, 8, 100, 4096, 65535, 65536, 70000, and `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict`\nwith a CDict built by `LZ4F_createCDict`. Also call `LZ4F_compressBegin_internal` directly.\nFor `usingDictOnce`, read the C to see how it differs from `usingDict` (the dictionary is\nonly applied to the first block) and design a MULTI-BLOCK test that actually distinguishes\nthem.\n\n**Context reuse:** run a second complete frame through the SAME cctx without freeing it\n(both with and without changing the preferences), because `cctx->totalInSize` is only reset\nwhen `contentSize != 0` and `maxBufferSize` only ever grows — so reuse is a distinct axis.\n\n**Input shapes:** all `N_SHAPES`; total sizes 0, 1, 2, 15, blockSize-1, blockSize,\nblockSize+1, several blocks, many blocks. Random data forces stored blocks; repetitive data\nforces long matches.\n\n## Error rows you own — assert the SAME error code via `lz4f_error_code`, not just \"failed\"\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` / `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` with `cStage != 1` (i.e. before any\n  `compressBegin`, and again after `compressEnd`) -> `compressionState_uninitialized` (20)\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin*` with `dstCapacity < 19` (`LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX`): sweep 0..=18\n  -> `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` (11); 19 must succeed\n- `LZ4F_compressUpdate` with `dstCapacity < LZ4F_compressBound(srcSize, prefs)`: sweep\n  small capacities -> `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` (11)\n- `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` with `dstCapacity < srcSize` -> `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` (11)\n  (this extra check applies only to the uncompressed path)\n- `LZ4F_flush` with `dstCapacity` smaller than `tmpInSize + blockHeader + blockFooter`\n  -> `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` (11)\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd` with `dstCapacity < 4`, and `< 8` when contentChecksum is enabled\n  -> `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` (11)\n- `LZ4F_compressEnd` when the declared `contentSize` does not match the bytes actually\n  supplied -> `frameSize_wrong` (14). Test BOTH too-few and too-many bytes.\n- `LZ4F_createCompressionContext(NULL, version)` -> `parameter_null` (21)\n- `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` with `dictSize > INT_MAX` (e.g. `0x8000_0000usize`) and a\n  non-NULL dictBuffer -> `parameter_invalid` (4). **Pass a small real buffer with a lying\n  size** — the C checks the size before touching the pointer (lz4frame.c:766-768), so this\n  is safe. VERIFY that in the C source first; if it is not safe, skip and say so.\n- Allocation failures -> `allocation_failed` (9) / NULL. These ARE testable via\n  `LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced` / `LZ4F_compressBegin*` with a `LZ4F_CustomMem`\n  whose `customAlloc`/`customCalloc` returns NULL — write `extern \"C\"` allocator callbacks\n  with a static counter so you can fail the Nth allocation and reach each distinct\n  allocation site (`LZ4F_cctx` calloc, `lz4CtxPtr` malloc, `tmpBuff` malloc). Assert BOTH\n  libraries return the same error / NULL. Make sure your allocator FREES correctly for the\n  calls you let succeed, so the test does not leak or double-free.\n- `LZ4F_freeCompressionContext(NULL)` -> accepted, returns `LZ4F_OK_NoError` (0)\n- Out-of-range enum values for `blockSizeID` / `blockMode` / `contentChecksumFlag` /\n  `blockChecksumFlag` / `frameType` passed across the FFI (C enums accept any int). Per the\n  C source the compress side masks the flags with `& 1` and does NOT validate them, and\n  `compressBegin` does NOT validate `blockSizeID` at all — so assert C and Rust agree on\n  the resulting bytes / errors rather than assuming an error.\n- A wrong `version` argument to `LZ4F_createCompressionContext*` (the C never checks it —\n  confirm and assert both accept it identically).\n\n## Deliverable\nWrite ONE file: `tests/lz4frame_stream_diff.rs`.\n\nMake it PASS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4frame_stream_diff 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nAlways `--release --offline`. Other agents build concurrently — if cargo blocks on the\ntarget lock, wait and retry. After ANY edit to `src/lz4frame.rs`, run\n`timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running.\nKeep runtime under ~180 s: byte-at-a-time updates over a 4 MB block are very slow, so use\nSMALL inputs for fine-grained chunking and large inputs only for coarse chunking, while\nKEEPING every axis covered.\n\nReport back: exact `#[test]` names, the final pass/fail line, every divergence found with\nthe precise C-vs-Rust difference and the fix you made to the Rust, and confirm which of\nyour 12 symbols you exercised.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ieCE1Y-translated-rust/5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b/tasks/a83afac96ffa104c1.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
