{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hyety2c22ugaeq667azrqvqedhv2jhn2eykhepqiopgc4ch3u6pa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `tests/lz4hc_diff.rs` (2926 lines) written and passing.\n\n## Final result\n```\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4hc_diff\ntest result: ok. 26 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 9.41s\n```\nRuntime: ~9.4 s parallel / ~19 s single-threaded — well under the 180 s budget.\n\n## The 26 `#[test]` functions\nMetadata / level axis\n- `hc_sizeof_state_and_stream_state`\n- `hc_levels_belowmin_and_lz4mid` (levels `i32::MIN`, -1, 0, 1, 2)\n- `hc_levels_hashchain_low` (3–6)\n- `hc_levels_hashchain_high` (7–9)\n- `hc_levels_optimal` (10, 11)\n- `hc_levels_optimal_ultra_and_above_max` (12, 13, 100, `i32::MAX`)\n\nState / one-shot\n- `hc_extstatehc_and_fastreset_state_reuse`\n- `hc_extstatehc_misaligned_state_returns_zero`\n- `hc_compress_hc_destsize_target_sweep`\n\nStreaming\n- `hc_create_free_init_and_reset_stream`\n- `hc_init_stream_invalid_buffers`\n- `hc_set_compression_level_out_of_range`\n- `hc_favor_decompression_speed_axis`\n- `hc_load_dict_size_axis`\n- `hc_continue_multiblock_prefix`\n- `hc_continue_multiblock_extdict`\n- `hc_continue_level_change_midstream`\n- `hc_continue_destsize`\n- `hc_save_dict_hc`\n- `hc_attach_hc_dictionary`\n- `hc_search_ext_dict_direct`\n\nDeprecated / legacy\n- `hc_deprecated_oneshot_and_withstate`\n- `hc_deprecated_streaming_and_legacy_state`\n\nError paths\n- `hc_error_dst_capacity_too_small`\n- `hc_error_srcsize_out_of_range`\n- `hc_randomized_property_loop` (900 iterations, fixed seed)\n\n## Symbol coverage — verified programmatically\nAll **35** global symbols defined by `lz4hc.c.o` are resolved via `both(...)` and called (script-diffed `nm -g --defined-only` against the test source; `NOT exercised: []`). That includes every deprecated entry point plus `LZ4_setCompressionLevel`, `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed`, and `LZ4HC_searchExtDict`.\n\n## Divergences found\n**None.** The Rust translation matched the C byte-for-byte on every axis, including full `LZ4HC_CCtx_internal` state blobs after each call. `src/lz4hc.rs` and everything in `c_src/` are unmodified (verified byte-identical / mtimes untouched).\n\nTwo initial failures were **bugs in my own harness**, not the Rust: I built the round-trip dictionary history as `dict[len-used..]`, but `LZ4_loadDictHC` keeps `dict[dictSize-used .. dictSize]` (it only drops a leading part when `dictSize > 64 KB`). Fixed in `hc_load_dict_size_axis` and `hc_attach_hc_dictionary`.\n\n## Notable implementation decisions\n- **`LZ4HC_searchExtDict` is called directly** through the FFI (returns `#[repr(C)] {off,len,back}`), with the exact argument shape its internal callers use (`gDictEndIndex == 64 KB`, `ipIndex == (ip-prefixStart)+dictLimit`, `dictCtx` = a `LZ4_loadDictHC`-prepared stream). The dictionary sits in the middle of a 3×64 KB arena so transient out-of-window `matchPtr` values stay mapped. A `nonempty > 0` counter guards against a vacuous pass.\n- **`c_src` is compiled without `-DNDEBUG`, so its `assert()`s are live.** `LZ4_compressHC2_continue` hard-codes `dstCapacity = 0` with `notLimited`, and `LZ4MID_compress` ends with `assert(op <= oend)` (lz4hc.c:743) — so levels 1/2 through that specific wrapper would abort the C build. Levels 1/2 are therefore driven through `LZ4_compressHC2_limitedOutput_continue` instead; documented in a comment.\n- **`srcSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` is tested for real, no 2 GB allocation**: the check at lz4hc.c:1390 is `(U32)*srcSizePtr > (U32)LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` and runs *before* any buffer access, and the unsigned cast also rejects negatives — so oversized and negative sizes are passed with 64-byte buffers.\n- **State comparison** uses full-blob `memcmp` of all 262192 bytes where both sides get the same input pointers, and a structural view (tables + pointer offsets relative to `prefixStart`) where they can't (`LZ4_saveDictHC`, `LZ4_attach_HC_dictionary`).\n- **Shared vs. per-library arenas**: extDict streaming uses one arena shared by both libs so `LZ4_compressHC_continue_generic`'s pointer-comparison overlap detection behaves identically; `saveDictHC` uses two arenas with identical layouts for the same reason.\n\n## Mutation-tested sensitivity\nI temporarily mutated `src/lz4hc.rs` twice to prove the comparison is live, then restored it byte-identically:\n- `LZ4_favorDecompressionSpeed`: `(favor != 0)` → `(favor > 1)` — caught by `hc_favor_decompression_speed_axis`.\n- `LZ4HC_literalsPrice`: `>= RUN_MASK` → `> RUN_MASK` — survived `hc_levels_optimal` (10/11) but was caught by 6 tests including `hc_levels_optimal_ultra_and_above_max`, `hc_compress_hc_destsize_target_sweep`, and `hc_randomized_property_loop`.\n\nNote: an unrelated pre-existing test in the workspace, `tests/lz4frame_oneshot_diff.rs` (not mine, appeared during this session), has 3 failures in a `usingCDict` frame path. `tests/lz4_block.rs`, `lz4_errors.rs`, `lz4_stream.rs`, and `lz4frame_decompress_diff.rs` all pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":253644,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":189,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DtEpphjB9VEgeb4dKuYnvc","session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"60ad1cfb-2e16-42bf-bd31-c0c6c0789d4f","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:43:04.838Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4hc differential tests"}
