{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yii5nlps7jse3y5guw6dvjlx57u6gtl6bxlt2gj4krgefrlotuxq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\n```\ntest result: ok. 25 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 6.02s\n```\n\nFiles touched (only these two):\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/tests/lz4frame_oneshot_diff.rs` (new, 2357 lines)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/src/lz4frame.rs` (two divergence fixes)\n\nRe-ran all pre-existing suites afterwards: `lz4_block` 10, `lz4_stream` 6, `lz4_errors` 20, `lz4hc_diff` 26, `xxhash_diff` 27, `symbol_parity` 3 — all still pass.\n\n## `#[test]` names (25)\n\n`version_and_compression_level_max`, `get_block_size_every_id_and_random`, `is_error_and_get_error_code`, `get_error_name_bytes_identical`, `bounds_null_prefs_and_full_cross_product`, `bounds_randomised_including_out_of_range_enums_and_huge_sizes`, `compress_frame_full_preference_cross_product`, `compress_frame_multiblock_preference_cross_product`, `compress_frame_blocksize_blockmode_checksum_cross_product`, `compress_frame_block_boundaries_64kb_all_shapes`, `compress_frame_dense_small_and_boundary_size_sweep`, `compress_frame_block_boundaries_large_ids`, `compress_frame_all_compression_level_regimes`, `compress_frame_frametype_favor_and_random_sizes`, `row_170_compress_frame_dst_too_small`, `compress_frame_null_prefs_and_null_src`, `compress_frame_out_of_range_enum_values`, `create_cdict_all_sizes_and_free_null`, `compress_frame_using_cdict_cross_product`, `create_cdict_truncates_to_last_64kb`, `compress_frame_using_cdict_null_dict_and_null_cctx`, `row_170_using_cdict_dst_too_small`, `rows_179_180_create_cdict_allocation_failure`, `header_size_on_real_frames_every_option_combination`, `header_size_truncations_skippable_magics_and_garbage`\n\n## Divergences found — both are the SAME root cause\n\nThe C enums `LZ4F_blockSizeID_t`, `LZ4F_blockMode_t`, `LZ4F_contentChecksum_t`, `LZ4F_blockChecksum_t`, `LZ4F_frameType_t` (lz4frame.h:123-161) have **only non-negative enumerators**, so GCC gives them a compatible type of **`unsigned int`**. The Rust translation declares those struct fields / parameters as `c_int` and therefore *signed*-compares and *sign*-extends them. Invisible for the in-range values 0/1/4..7, but observable for any out-of-range value arriving over the ABI.\n\n**Divergence 1 — `LZ4F_compressBound_internal` (lz4frame.c:398-399)**\nRepro: `LZ4F_compressFrameBound(2480036, {blockSizeID=6, contentChecksumFlag=-1, blockChecksumFlag=-1, autoFlush=1})` → **C = 68721956791, Rust = 2480055**. C computes `BFSize * (unsigned)4294967295` (zero-extended → `0x3FFFFFFFC`); Rust computed `BFSize * (usize)(-1)` (sign-extended → `-4`).\nFix in `src/lz4frame.rs`:\n```rust\nlet blockCRCSize: usize =\n    BFSize.wrapping_mul((*prefsPtr).frameInfo.blockChecksumFlag as u32 as usize);\nlet frameEnd: usize = BHSize.wrapping_add(\n    ((*prefsPtr).frameInfo.contentChecksumFlag as u32 as usize).wrapping_mul(BFSize),\n);\n```\n(was `... as usize`, i.e. sign-extending).\n\n**Divergence 2 — `LZ4F_optimalBSID` (lz4frame.c:364)**\nRepro: `LZ4F_compressFrame(..., srcSize=0, prefs.blockSizeID = -2)` → C frame `04224d18 60 40 82...`, Rust `04224d18 60 60 51...` — the **BD header byte differed (0x40 vs 0x60)**. `while (requestedBSID > proposedBSID)` is an unsigned comparison in C, so `-2` (== 4294967294) enters the loop and gets normalised to `LZ4F_max64KB`; the Rust returned `-2` unchanged, which then landed in the BD byte as `(-2 & 7) << 4 == 0x60` and made `maxBlockSize` an error sentinel.\nFix:\n```rust\nwhile (requestedBSID as u32) > (proposedBSID as u32) {\n```\n\nI deliberately did **not** change `LZ4F_getBlockSize`'s `blockSizeID < LZ4F_max64KB || blockSizeID > LZ4F_max4MB`: the C's unsigned comparison and the Rust's signed one reject exactly the same set of IDs with the same `maxBlockSize_invalid` value, so it is not observable (verified over all of `-8..=16`, `i32::MIN/MAX` and 40 000 randomised ints).\n\n## Third failure — a C property, not a divergence\n\n`compress_frame_using_cdict_cross_product` initially failed with `LZ4F_decompress` error 16 in **both** libraries on byte-identical frames: a `LZ4F_CDict` is not recorded in the frame, so such frames must be decoded with `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`. Fixed in the test (`round_trip_both_with_dict`, which also mirrors the CDict's last-64 KB truncation).\n\n## Coverage of the 14 symbols\n\nAll 14 exercised through the `.so` export tables via `both::<T>()`:\n- **`LZ4F_getVersion`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`** — value + repeat-stability, pinned to 100 / 12.\n- **`LZ4F_getBlockSize`** — every int in `-8..=16`, `i32::MIN/MAX`, `±0x7FFFFFFF`, 40 000 randomised ints; rows 168/169 assert `maxBlockSize_invalid == 2` in both.\n- **`LZ4F_isError` / `LZ4F_getErrorCode`** — 0, 1, 100, `-(size_t)code` for 0..=24, `-25`, `-100`, `usize::MAX`, `usize::MAX/2`, `1<<63`, ~6 000 randoms; also cross-checked against the harness's re-implementations, and the `-(maxCode)` boundary pinned.\n- **`LZ4F_getErrorName`** — same probe set + extra out-of-range codes, compared as `CStr::to_bytes()`; four concrete strings pinned.\n- **`LZ4F_compressFrameBound` / `LZ4F_compressBound`** — NULL prefs; the full 7040-combination cross product (blockSizeID{0,4,5,6,7} × blockMode × contentChecksum × blockChecksum × autoFlush × contentSize × dictID{0,0xDEADBEEF} × 11 levels) over 12 srcSizes; plus 30 000 randomised cases including out-of-range enums and `usize::MAX`-region sizes (wrap-around parity).\n- **`LZ4F_compressFrame`** — full 7040-combination cross product at 2 KB and a 384-combination multi-block cross product at 70 KB/300 KB; the 40 blockSizeID×blockMode×both-checksum combos at sizes that actually keep each blockSizeID (70 K/70 K/300 K/1.2 M/5 M); dense srcSize sweep (`0..=80`, `bs±8`, `2·bs±8`); `blockSize−1/blockSize/blockSize+1/2·blockSize+7` for every blockSizeID with `blockSize` derived from `LZ4F_getBlockSize`; all `N_SHAPES`; 14 levels spanning `i32::MIN`, −1000, −1, 0, 1 (LZ4-fast), 2 (lz4mid), 3..9 (hashChain), 10..12 (optimal), 13, `i32::MAX`; `frameType` both values; `favorDecSpeed` both; 600 randomised cases; `dstCapacity == bound` and `bound + 37` compared byte-for-byte; every success round-tripped through both libs' `LZ4F_decompress`.\n- **`LZ4F_createCDict` / `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` / `LZ4F_freeCDict`** — dict sizes 0/1/8/100/4096/65535/65536/70000 × 6 shapes for both constructors; `LZ4F_freeCDict(NULL)`; explicit proof that a 70 000-byte dict behaves as its last 64 KB.\n- **`LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict`** — 800 cases (8 dict sizes × plain/advanced × 5 (bsid,len) × 10 levels), byte-identical + round-tripped with `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict`; `cdict == NULL` proven byte-identical to `LZ4F_compressFrame`; NULL `cctx` with `dstCapacity < 19` (safe per lz4frame.c:456, checked before any cctx deref) → `dstMaxSize_tooSmall` in both.\n- **`LZ4F_headerSize`** — real frames from all 160 header-relevant option combos (all four header lengths 7/11/15/19 produced and asserted), truncations at every length `0..=19` on 7-byte and 19-byte headers, `NULL` src → `srcPtr_wrong(15)`, all 16 skippable magics `0x184D2A50..=0x184D2A5F` → 8, adjacent non-skippable magics → `frameType_unknown(13)`, all 256 FLG bytes behind a valid magic, and 4 000 garbage/random buffers.\n\n## Error rows\n\n- rows **168/169** — `maxBlockSize_invalid(2)` for every invalid ID in both.\n- row **170** — `dstMaxSize_tooSmall(11)`, capacity swept 0..bound−1 (exhaustively when bound ≤ 600) for 5 `compressFrame` pref sets and 4 `_usingCDict` sets; also asserts dst is left entirely 0xAA on that path, and that exactly `bound` succeeds. Minimal repro `srcSize=0, cap=0` pinned.\n- rows **179/180** — forced via `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` with a counting `LZ4F_CustomMem`: each of the four internal