{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_it6k2azlejaivwqinczfjh5zgihvvbljbswyxtiecyoc6uuvyrkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both deliverables are written and passing.\n\n## Files\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/tests/lz4frame_decompress_diff.rs` (3161 lines, 24 tests)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust/tests/lz4file_diff.rs` (1399 lines, 9 tests)\n\nNothing in `c_src/` or `src/` was touched.\n\n## Final results\n\n```\ntest result: ok. 24 passed; 0 failed; ... finished in 13.84s   (lz4frame_decompress_diff)\ntest result: ok.  9 passed; 0 failed; ... finished in  1.46s   (lz4file_diff)\n```\n\n`#[test]` names — `lz4frame_decompress_diff.rs`: `dctx_lifecycle_create_reset_free`, `get_block_size_all_ids`, `header_size_real_headers_and_truncations`, `get_frame_info_before_decompress`, `get_frame_info_midstream`, `decompress_one_shot_option_matrix`, `decompress_src_chunk_granularity`, `decompress_dst_capacity_granularity`, `decompress_src_dst_cross_product`, `decompress_random_chunking`, `decompress_options_axes`, `decompress_large_multiblock_frames`, `decompress_all_compression_levels`, `decompress_using_dict_axes`, `decompress_uncompressed_blocks`, `decompress_skippable_frames`, `decompress_multi_frame`, `decompress_tiny_and_boundary_sizes`, `decompress_error_paths`, `decompress_recycled_dst_buffer`, `decompress_entering_at_dstage_init`, `get_frame_info_during_skippable_skip`, `decompress_wrong_content_size`, `harness_self_check_detects_divergence`.\n\n`lz4file_diff.rs`: `write_preferences_matrix`, `write_call_size_axes`, `write_content_size_enforcement`, `read_size_axes`, `write_read_cross_libraries`, `read_multiframe_skippable_and_eof`, `read_src_buffer_sizing_across_frames`, `lz4file_error_paths`, `harness_self_check_detects_divergence`.\n\n## Divergences found: none\n\nThe Rust translation of `lz4frame.c`'s decompressor and all of `lz4file.c` is byte-for-byte equivalent to the C across everything I threw at it — no Rust edits were needed. Because \"zero divergences\" is a suspicious result, I added two permanent guards so the suites cannot pass vacuously:\n\n1. `api()` asserts the C and Rust `LZ4F_decompress` / `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` / `LZ4F_headerSize` / `LZ4F_write` / `LZ4F_read` function pointers are at *distinct* addresses (i.e. two real libraries are loaded).\n2. `harness_self_check_detects_divergence` (`#[should_panic]`, in both files) deliberately feeds the Rust side a bit-flipped frame and asserts the comparison machinery fires.\n\nTwo C behaviours I had to accommodate in the *tests* (correct C, not bugs): `LZ4F_readOpen` does an unconditional `fread(buf,1,19,fp)` and returns `io_read` for any file shorter than `LZ4F_HEADER_SIZE_MAX`, so `.lz4` files < 19 bytes are unopenable (`expect_readback` asserts exactly that); and `LZ4F_compressBegin` ignores `frameType`, so skippable frames must be hand-crafted.\n\n## dStage coverage\n\nAll 15 `dStage_t` states are reached, each documented in the file header comment with the configuration that reaches it: `getFrameHeader` (both the `>=maxFHSize` shortcut and the fall-through), `storeFrameHeader`, `init`, `getBlockHeader`, `storeBlockHeader`, `copyDirect` (incl. the partial `tmpInTarget -= sizeToCopy` return), `getBlockChecksum` (both the \"4 bytes ready\" and byte-at-a-time `dctx->header` accumulation paths), `getCBlock`, `storeCBlock`, `flushOut` (incl. partial flush), `getSuffix`, `storeSuffix`, `getSFrameSize`, `storeSFrameSize` (both entries — via `storeFrameHeader` when `LZ4F_decodeHeader` runs on `dctx->header`, and via `getSFrameSize` with <4 bytes left), `skipSkippable`. Every state is also hit as the *entry* state of a fresh call, except `getSuffix`, which the C state machine can only reach by fall-through; `init`-as-entry required decoding the header with `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` first (`decompress_entering_at_dstage_init`).\n\nThe highest-value axis I added beyond the brief: destination geometry is swept **two** ways, because they drive disjoint `LZ4F_updateDict()` branches — an *advancing* dst pointer (history stays in prefix mode inside the caller's buffer) and a *recycled* dst buffer, the classic streaming pattern, which forces the decoder to migrate the 64 KB history into `tmpOutBuffer` and covers \"continue history within tmpOutBuffer\", \"copy relevant dict portion in front of tmpOut\", \"copy dst into tmp to complete dict\", \"join dict & dest into tmp\", the `dictSize > 128 KB` truncation, and the end-of-call \"preserve history within tmpOut\" block in both its `flushOut` and non-`flushOut` forms.\n\n`decompress_wrong_content_size` splices a valid 19-byte header declaring `contentSize = A` onto the body of a frame carrying `B != A` bytes, which reaches `LZ4F_ERROR_frameSize_wrong` at `dstage_getSuffix` exactly (asserted) and specifically exercises the wrap-around of `frameRemainingSize -= n`. `decompress_error_paths` additionally runs 12 000 seeded bit-flip/truncation mutants, and `lz4file_error_paths` runs 2 500."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2155,"cache_read_input_tokens":371504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2155,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016UzAKZwKyMNJCsJYRtsyw8","session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"1a8dd899-ce88-4db0-b921-78a88f86e7c6","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:59:27.655Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lz4frame decompression tests"}
