{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nlomcpo3g7nh3c72femvqe5hx56fpxja5wpc4iqh3j3nmr5qbnmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01MKYk4UMDTn1UfVtVFpWvXe","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Phase C row tests for lz4frame","prompt":"Write row-by-row Phase C error-path differential tests for lz4frame.c.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\n## Your exact job\n`ERRORS.md` in the crate root is the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE, derived mechanically from the C\nsource. **Rows 168–221 are the `## lz4frame.c` section and they are YOUR assignment.**\nRead those 54 rows. For EVERY ONE, write a test that constructs that exact invalid\ninput/condition, calls BOTH the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`, and asserts they return the\nSAME error code / sentinel — not merely \"both failed somehow\". For LZ4F functions that\nmeans asserting the identical `LZ4F_getErrorCode()` value, e.g. `err::ERROR_dstMaxSize_tooSmall`\n(11), not just `lz4f_is_error(x) == true`.\n\nDeliverable: ONE new file `tests/lz4frame_errors.rs`.\n\nDo NOT edit any other test file. If you find a genuine C-vs-Rust divergence, fix\n`src/lz4frame.rs` (the C is ALWAYS correct). DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN `c_src/`.\n\n## Context\n- C ground truth: `c_src/src/lz4frame.c`, `c_src/include/lz4frame.h`, `lz4frame_static.h`\n- Rust: `src/lz4frame.rs`\n- Built libs: C = `c_src/build/liblz4.so`, Rust = `target/release/liblz4.so`\n\n## MANDATORY harness\nREAD `tests/common/mod.rs` first. Also read `tests/lz4_errors.rs` — it is the EXACT\nmodel for what I want, including how it documents rows it deliberately does not test.\nAlso skim `tests/lz4frame_stream_diff.rs` and `tests/lz4frame_oneshot_diff.rs` so you\ndon't duplicate what already exists (but DO still write a row-labelled test for each\nrow; cross-reference the existing test by name in a comment if it already covers it).\n\nHarness API:\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way to obtain functions.\n  NEVER call Rust code directly, never `use lz4::...`.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`, `gen_shape`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name`\n- `assert_bytes_eq(ctx, c, r)`\n- `LZ4F_frameInfo_t`, `LZ4F_preferences_t` (Default == LZ4F_INIT_PREFERENCES),\n  `LZ4F_compressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`, `LZ4F_CustomMem`\n- all `LZ4F_*` constants; `lz4f_is_error(code)`, `lz4f_error_code(code)`, `err::*`\n- **HARNESS RULE**: pre-fill the C dst buffer and the Rust dst buffer with the SAME\n  sentinel byte (`0xAA`) and compare the FULL buffer. Different fills = false positives.\n- Write hex literals carefully: `0xF1LL`, `0x1EVE_1234` etc. are INVALID Rust. Use only\n  0-9a-fA-F and `_`.\n\n## Naming and traceability — REQUIRED\nName each test so the row is obvious, e.g. `row_168_169_get_block_size_invalid_id`,\n`row_181_update_before_begin`. Group several closely-related rows in one `#[test]` when\nnatural, but the function name and inline comments MUST cite every row number covered.\nAt the END of the file add a comment block listing EVERY row 168–221 and, for each, either\nthe test function that covers it or the precise reason it cannot be tested. Valid reasons\n(and ONLY these):\n- the code is not compiled into the library under test (e.g. `LZ4F_HEAPMODE=0` in\n  `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` removes a branch)\n- the C documents it as `assert`-only / undefined behaviour, so calling it faults both\n  libraries identically and proves nothing (say which assert, with the line number)\n- it is a compile-time `#error` / static assert (both libraries built, which is the proof)\nDo NOT use \"hard to test\" as a reason. Allocation-failure rows ARE testable here: rows\n172/173/177/178/179/180 can be forced with `LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced` /\n`LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` and an `LZ4F_CustomMem` whose `customAlloc`/`customCalloc`\nreturns NULL on the Nth call — write `extern \"C\"` callbacks with a static counter, and\nmake sure you `free` whatever you did allocate so the test neither leaks nor double-frees.\n\n## Two important, already-established C facts — do not re-litigate them\n1. `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` is only supported with `LZ4F_blockIndependent`\n   (lz4frame.h:707). The `blockLinked` path hits `assert(blockCompression ==\n   LZ4B_COMPRESSED)` (lz4frame.c:1071) and corrupts the heap INSIDE THE C. Do not drive it.\n2. `LZ4F_compressUpdateImpl` checks `dstCapacity` BEFORE `LZ4F_flush()` on a\n   blockCompressMode switch and then advances `dstPtr` without deducting the flushed\n   bytes (lz4frame.c:1006-1016), so the C can legitimately write and RETURN MORE than\n   `dstCapacity`. If you drive that path, allocate a large slack region past\n   `dstCapacity` (see `Sess::SLACK` in `tests/lz4frame_stream_diff.rs`) so the overrun\n   lands in your own allocation. `tests/lz4frame_dstcapacity_overrun.rs` already pins it.\n\nAlso note the C enums (`LZ4F_blockSizeID_t` etc.) have only non-negative enumerators, so\nGCC's compatible type is **unsigned int**. Two real bugs were already found and fixed from\nthis. Include rows that pass out-of-range enum values across the FFI.\n\n## Make it pass\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4frame_errors 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nAlways `--release --offline`. After ANY edit to `src/lz4frame.rs` run\n`timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running, then ALSO re-run the\nexisting suites to be sure you broke nothing:\n`timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline 2>&1 | grep -E 'Running|test result'`\nKeep your file's runtime under ~120 s.\n\nReport back: the exact `#[test]` names, the final pass/fail line, a row-by-row table of\n168–221 -> covering test (or documented reason), any divergence found and the fix you made\nto the Rust, and confirmation that the whole suite still passes."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2191,"cache_read_input_tokens":343428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"5f6d9e64-7196-4de1-b847-249073272069","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:10:27.997Z"}
