 after a prior failure (`compressionState_uninitialized`, row 14) — lz4file.c:296-303 | the `LZ4F_compressUpdate()` error is returned verbatim; additionally `lz4fWrite->errCode` is latched to that error, which makes a later `LZ4F_writeClose()` skip `LZ4F_compressEnd()` (see row 82) |\n89\t| 246 | `LZ4F_write` | `fwrite(dstBuf, 1, ret, fp) != ret` for a compressed chunk — lz4file.c:305-308 | error `LZ4F_ERROR_io_write` (`LZ4F_getErrorCode()==22`); `lz4fWrite->errCode` latched to the same value |\n90\t| 247 | `LZ4F_writeClose` | `lz4fWrite == NULL` — lz4file.c:321-323 | error `LZ4F_ERROR_parameter_null` (`LZ4F_getErrorCode()==21`) |\n91\t| 248 | `LZ4F_writeClose` | `LZ4F_compressEnd(cctx, dstBuf, dstBufMaxSize, NULL)` fails — lz4file.c:326-331. Reachable: `frameSize_wrong` (row 23) when `prefsPtr->frameInfo.contentSize` was declared at `LZ4F_writeOpen()` and the total bytes passed to `LZ4F_write()` differ | the `LZ4F_compressEnd()` error is returned verbatim (e.g. `LZ4F_ERROR_frameSize_wrong`, code 14); the handle is still freed via the `out:` label |\n92\t| 249 | `LZ4F_writeClose` | `lz4fWrite->errCode != LZ4F_OK_NoError` (a previous `LZ4F_write()` failed, row 78/79): the whole finalize block is skipped — lz4file.c:325 | returns `LZ4F_OK_NoError` (0) — the previously latched error is **silently discarded**, and no endMark/content checksum is written, leaving a truncated frame on disk. The handle is freed |\n93\t| 250 | `LZ4F_writeClose` | `fwrite(dstBuf, 1, ret, fp) != ret` when writing the frame footer (endMark + optional content checksum) — lz4file.c:333-335 | returns `returnErrorCode(LZ4F_ERROR_io_write)` = error `LZ4F_ERROR_io_write` (`LZ4F_getErrorCode()==22`); the handle is still freed |\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t## LZ4F_errorCodes enum values\n97\t\n98\tDerived from the `LZ4F_LIST_ERRORS(ITEM)` macro order in `c_src/include/lz4frame.h:653-678`\n99\t(expanded by `LZ4F_GENERATE_ENUM` into a plain C enum, so values are sequential from 0):\n100\t\n101\t| value | constant |\n102\t|---|---|\n103\t| 0 | `LZ4F_OK_NoError` |\n104\t| 1 | `LZ4F_ERROR_GENERIC` |\n105\t| 2 | `LZ4F_ERROR_maxBlockSize_invalid` |\n106\t| 3 | `LZ4F_ERROR_blockMode_invalid` |\n107\t| 4 | `LZ4F_ERROR_parameter_invalid` |\n108\t| 5 | `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionLevel_invalid` |\n109\t| 6 | `LZ4F_ERROR_headerVersion_wrong` |\n110\t| 7 | `LZ4F_ERROR_blockChecksum_invalid` |\n111\t| 8 | `LZ4F_ERROR_reservedFlag_set` |\n112\t| 9 | `LZ4F_ERROR_allocation_failed` |\n113\t| 10 | `LZ4F_ERROR_srcSize_tooLarge` |\n114\t| 11 | `LZ4F_ERROR_dstMaxSize_tooSmall` |\n115\t| 12 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameHeader_incomplete` |\n116\t| 13 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameType_unknown` |\n117\t| 14 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameSize_wrong` |\n118\t| 15 | `LZ4F_ERROR_srcPtr_wrong` |\n119\t| 16 | `LZ4F_ERROR_decompressionFailed` |\n120\t| 17 | `LZ4F_ERROR_headerChecksum_invalid` |\n121\t| 18 | `LZ4F_ERROR_contentChecksum_invalid` |\n122\t| 19 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameDecoding_alreadyStarted` |\n123\t| 20 | `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionState_uninitialized` |\n124\t| 21 | `LZ4F_ERROR_parameter_null` |\n125\t| 22 | `LZ4F_ERROR_io_write` |\n126\t| 23 | `LZ4F_ERROR_io_read` |\n127\t| 24 | `LZ4F_ERROR_maxCode` |\n128\t\n129\t`LZ4F_isError(code)` is `code > (size_t)(-LZ4F_ERROR_maxCode)`, i.e. true only for\n130\t`code` in `[-(size_t)23 .. -(size_t)1]` (SIZE_MAX-22 .. SIZE_MAX). `-(size_t)24` (maxCode)\n131\titself is **not** reported as an error, and `LZ4F_getErrorName()` indexes\n132\t`LZ4F_errorStrings[-(int)code]`, which is in range 1..23 for all real errors.\n133\t\n134\t\n135\t## Notes: checks that do NOT exist in these two files\n136\t\n137\tThese are recorded so the test suite does not assert behaviour the C code never implements.\n138\t\n139\t- **Never raised anywhere in `lz4frame.c` / `lz4file.c`**: `LZ4F_ERROR_GENERIC` (1),\n140\t  `LZ4F_ERROR_blockMode_invalid` (3), `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionLevel_invalid` (5),\n141\t  `LZ4F_ERROR_srcSize_tooLarge` (10). Verified by grep; the constants exist only in the enum.\n142\t- **No compressionLevel validation.** `prefs.compressionLevel` is only compared against\n143\t  `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN` (2) to pick fast vs HC context (lz4frame.c:705, 711, 728, 763, 956, 967).\n144\t  Negative values become an LZ4 `acceleration` (lz4frame.c:913, 925); values above\n145\t  `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX` (12) are clamped inside lz4hc. No error is ever returned.\n146\t- **No blockMode / contentChecksumFlag / blockChecksumFlag enum validation on the compress\n147\t  side.** They are masked into the FLG byte with `& _1BIT` (lz4frame.c:788-791), so out-of-range\n148\t  values silently alias to 0/1.\n149\t- **`LZ4F_compressBegin*` does not validate `frameInfo.blockSizeID`.** At lz4frame.c:740 the\n150\t  result of `LZ4F_getBlockSize()` is assigned to `cctx->maxBlockSize` **without** an error check,\n151\t  so e.g. `blockSizeID == 3` produces a huge `maxBlockSize` and a frame header carrying an\n152\t  illegal BD nibble instead of `maxBlockSize_invalid`. (The `LZ4F_compressFrame*` path is also\n153\t  unaffected because `LZ4F_compressBound_internal()` swallows the same error value.)\n154\t- **`LZ4F_createCompressionContext` / `LZ4F_createDecompressionContext` do not check `version`.**\n155\t  The `version` argument is merely stored into `cctx->version` / `dctx->version`\n156\t  (lz4frame.c:603, 1290) and never compared against `LZ4F_VERSION` (100); passing a wrong\n157\t  version is accepted silently. Same for the `_advanced` variants.\n158\t- **`LZ4F_compressEnd` does not check `cStage`.** When `tmpInSize == 0`, `LZ4F_flush()` returns 0\n159\t  before its state check (lz4frame.c:1167), so `LZ4F_compressEnd()` on a never-begun cctx emits a\n160\t  bare endMark instead of `compressionState_uninitialized`.\n161\t- **`LZ4F_decompress` / `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` / `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` do not NULL-check\n162\t  `dctx`, `srcSizePtr` or `dstSizePtr`** (only a debug `assert(dctx != NULL)` at lz4frame.c:1637);\n163\t  passing NULL is undefined behaviour, not an error code.\n164\t- **`LZ4F_compressUpdate` / `LZ4F_flush` / `LZ4F_compressEnd` do not NULL-check `cctx`.**\n165\t- **`LZ4F_freeCompressionContext` / `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` / `LZ4F_freeCDict` accept NULL**\n166\t  (lz4frame.c:631, 1316, 583) and return `LZ4F_OK_NoError`.\n167\t- Debug-only `assert()`s that are **internal invariants**, not reachable through any public API\n168\t  input, and therefore not table rows: lz4frame.c:462, 467, 472 (`dstEnd >= dstPtr`), 767\n169\t  (`cdict == NULL` when `dictBuffer != NULL` — no public entry passes both), 774\n170\t  (`lz4CtxType == ctxHC`), 891 (`compress != NULL`), 1024 (`blockSize > tmpInSize`), 1076, 1089,\n171\t  1181 (\"flush overflows dstBuffer!\"), 1218 (`flushSize <= dstCapacity`), 1415\n172\t  (`frameHeaderSize > 5`), 1531, 1533, 1540, 1547, 1550, 1554 (`LZ4F_updateDict` invariants),\n173\t  1872 (`tmpInTarget >= 4`), 1874 (`selectedIn != NULL`), 1895 (`dstPtr != NULL`), 2095\n174\t  (`tmpOutBuffer != NULL`); and lz4file.c:68, 212 (`statePtr != NULL`, always `&caller's ptr`\n175\t  which was already NULL-checked).\n176\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MKYk4UMDTn1UfVtVFpWvXe","session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"8e4ea1e4-f232-4271-a57c-3ffca9b98213","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:10:44.253Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C row tests for lz4frame"}
