{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sk6l5jbzcagw55tygxlozqnyhhxrlxkpcyr4j3a4j6epig6cn32q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Qh5LpfswRHc3cj7snaSEFQ","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Phase C row tests for lz4hc + xxhash","prompt":"Write row-by-row Phase C error-path differential tests for lz4hc.c and xxhash.c.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\n\n## Your exact job\n`ERRORS.md` in the crate root is the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE, derived mechanically from the C\nsource. **Rows 94–147 are `## lz4hc.c` and rows 148–167 are `## xxhash.c`. Those 74 rows\nare YOUR assignment.** Read them all. For EVERY ONE, write a test that constructs that\nexact invalid input/condition, calls BOTH the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`, and asserts they\nreturn the SAME error code / sentinel — not merely \"both failed somehow\" (e.g. exactly\n`0`, exactly `-1`, exactly `NULL`, exactly `XXH_ERROR` (1), or the exact clamped value for\nthe silent-clamp rows).\n\nDeliverable: ONE new file `tests/lz4hc_xxhash_errors.rs`.\n\nDo NOT edit any other test file. If you find a genuine C-vs-Rust divergence, fix\n`src/lz4hc.rs` or `src/xxhash.rs` (the C is ALWAYS correct). DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING IN\n`c_src/`.\n\n## Context\n- C ground truth: `c_src/src/lz4hc.c` + `c_src/include/lz4hc.h`,\n  `c_src/src/xxhash.c` + `c_src/include/xxhash.h`\n- Rust: `src/lz4hc.rs`, `src/xxhash.rs`\n- Built libs: C = `c_src/build/liblz4.so`, Rust = `target/release/liblz4.so`\n- xxhash is compiled with `-DXXH_NAMESPACE=LZ4_`, so the exported names are\n  `LZ4_XXH32`, `LZ4_XXH64`, `LZ4_XXH32_reset`, … `LZ4_XXH_versionNumber`.\n\n## MANDATORY harness\nREAD `tests/common/mod.rs` first. Read `tests/lz4_errors.rs` — it is the EXACT model for\nwhat I want, including how it documents rows it deliberately does not test. Also read the\nexisting `tests/lz4hc_diff.rs` and `tests/xxhash_diff.rs` so you don't duplicate them (but\nDO still write a row-labelled test per row; cross-reference the existing test by name in a\ncomment if it already covers that row).\n\nHarness API:\n- `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (c_fn, rust_fn)` — the ONLY way to obtain functions.\n  NEVER call Rust code directly, never `use lz4::...`.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`, `gen_shape`, `N_SHAPES`, `shape_name`, `assert_bytes_eq`\n- `AlignedBuf::new(len, align)` / `AlignedBuf::with_offset(len, align, offset)` for\n  deliberately MISALIGNED pointers (needed for the `LZ4_initStreamHC` /\n  `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC` alignment rows)\n- constants `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN`(2), `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT`(9), `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_OPT_MIN`(10),\n  `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX`(12), `LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE`(0x7E000000), `XXH_OK`(0), `XXH_ERROR`(1),\n  `XXH32_canonical_t`, `XXH64_canonical_t`\n- **HARNESS RULE**: pre-fill the C dst buffer and the Rust dst buffer with the SAME\n  sentinel byte (`0xAA`) and compare the FULL buffer. Different fills = false positives.\n- Write hex literals carefully: `0xF1LL`, `0x1EVE_1234` etc. are INVALID Rust. Use only\n  0-9a-fA-F and `_`.\n\n## Facts already established — use them, don't re-derive\n- `LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MIN == 2`, and lz4hc has **THREE** strategies: levels 1–2 -> `lz4mid`\n  (`LZ4MID_compress`), 3–9 -> `LZ4HC_compress_hashChain`, 10–12 -> `LZ4HC_compress_optimal`.\n  `cLevel < 1` clamps to **9**, not to CLEVEL_MIN (`LZ4HC_getCLevelParams`, lz4hc.c:112).\n- `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` returns **1 on error**, not 0 (lz4hc.c:2153) — inverted vs\n  every other function.\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC*` explicitly `return 0` for a misaligned/NULL state\n  (lz4hc.c:1503, 1515) — unlike the lz4.c equivalents which are assert-only. Test these.\n- `srcSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` is testable WITHOUT a 2 GB allocation: the check at\n  lz4hc.c:1390 is `(U32)*srcSizePtr > (U32)LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` and runs BEFORE any buffer\n  access, and the unsigned cast also rejects negatives. Pass a lying size with a small\n  buffer. VERIFY that in the C source for each entry point before relying on it.\n- `LZ4_compressHC2_continue` / `_limitedOutput_continue` bypass auto-init and hard-code\n  `dstCapacity = 0` with the `notLimited` directive. The C is compiled WITHOUT `-DNDEBUG`,\n  so its `assert()`s are LIVE: `LZ4MID_compress` ends with `assert(op <= oend)`\n  (lz4hc.c:743), so levels 1/2 through `LZ4_compressHC2_continue` would abort the C.\n  Avoid that specific combination and say so in a comment.\n- xxhash: only `XXH32/64_update` validate anything (`input == NULL` -> `XXH_ERROR`,\n  because `XXH_ACCEPT_NULL_INPUT_POINTER == 0`). `reset`, `copyState`, `digest`,\n  `canonicalFromHash`, `hashFromCanonical` have **no** NULL check on the *state* pointer,\n  so passing NULL there is a guaranteed segfault in the C — document, do not test.\n  `freeState(NULL)` returns `XXH_OK` and IS testable.\n- Silent clamps that must be asserted as CLAMPS (not errors): HC level (9 / 12),\n  `LZ4_loadDictHC` / `LZ4_saveDictHC` 64 KB truncation,\n  `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` input truncation with `*srcSizePtr` rewritten.\n\n## Naming and traceability — REQUIRED\nName each test so the row is obvious, e.g. `row_104_108_extstatehc_null_and_misaligned`,\n`row_151_xxh32_total_len_wraparound`. Group closely related rows in one `#[test]` when\nnatural, but the function name and inline comments MUST cite every row number covered.\nAt the END of the file add a comment block listing EVERY row 94–167 with either its\ncovering test function or the precise reason it cannot be tested. Valid reasons (and ONLY\nthese):\n- the C documents it as `assert`-only / undefined behaviour, so calling it faults both\n  libraries identically and proves nothing (say which assert, with the line number)\n- the branch is unreachable on this x86-64 build (e.g. 32-bit-only code)\n- the code is not compiled into the library under test\n- compile-time `#error` / static assert (both libraries built, which is the proof)\n- reaching it requires an allocation near 2^31/2^64 that cannot be made on this machine\nDo NOT use \"hard to test\" as a reason.\n\n## Make it pass\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ieCE1Y/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4hc_xxhash_errors 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nAlways `--release --offline`. Other agents may build concurrently — if cargo blocks on the\ntarget lock, wait and retry. After ANY edit to `src/lz4hc.rs` or `src/xxhash.rs` run\n`timeout 600 cargo build --release --offline` before re-running, then re-run the existing\nsuites: `timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test lz4hc_diff --test xxhash_diff`.\nKeep runtime under ~150 s (HC level 12 is slow).\n\nReport back: the exact `#[test]` names, the final pass/fail line, a row-by-row table of\n94–167 -> covering test (or documented reason), and any divergence found plus the fix."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7260,"cache_read_input_tokens":345619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7260,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"562d0493-52a9-4d26-a237-30537f98c172","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:11:27.297Z"}
