{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hmqss3yz2nmqdgranyousinlk6ehd2s5myfzcasejevaezqeekha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four completion-gate criteria hold, independently re-verified after a clean rebuild.\n\n## Results\n\n**250 tests across 14 binaries, 0 failures.** Every call goes through both `.so` export tables via `libloading` — no test imports the crate (verified 0 occurrences), so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are tested too.\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 143 C symbols, 143 Rust, **0 missing / 0 extra**, 0 unresolved non-libc. All 143 also *exercised* by a test |\n| Phase B — `CONFIGS.md` | **240/240 rows `[x]`**, each driven with seeded randomized inputs |\n| Phase C — `ERRORS.md` | **250/250 rows accounted for**: 198 with a same-error-code differential test, 52 not observable with a verified reason |\n| Phase D — features | `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` → exactly 1 combination; `check_all_features.sh` derives the power set mechanically and passes `check` and `test` |\n\n## Two real translation bugs found and fixed\n\nBoth were the same root cause — **out-of-range C enum values crossing the FFI boundary**. `LZ4F_blockSizeID_t` et al. have only non-negative enumerators, so GCC's compatible type is `unsigned int`; the Rust modelled them as `c_int` and compared/extended them *signed*. I confirmed the signedness with a probe compiled against the real header before accepting the fixes:\n\n1. `LZ4F_compressBound_internal` — with `blockChecksumFlag = -1`, C returned `68721956791`, Rust `2480055` (sign- vs zero-extension into a 64-bit multiply).\n2. `LZ4F_optimalBSID` — `blockSizeID = -2` normalises to `LZ4F_max64KB` in C's unsigned loop; Rust passed `-2` through, corrupting the frame header's BD byte (`0x60` vs `0x40`).\n\n## Things worth flagging\n\n**I found a genuine buffer-overrun bug in the upstream C**, which the Rust reproduces exactly: `LZ4F_compressUpdateImpl` checks `dstCapacity` *before* the mode-switch `LZ4F_flush()`, then advances `dstPtr` without deducting the flushed bytes. Measured: `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate(srcSize=65536, dstCapacity=65560)` returns **65574**. This was aborting the test process via heap corruption until I added a slack region; it's now pinned by a dedicated regression test.\n\n**Three failures were wrong test expectations, not divergences** — the C/Rust comparison had already passed in each case. Rather than \"fix\" them, I traced each to the C and documented the real behaviour: `LZ4_resetStream_fast` deliberately re-uses the hash table (so a reused cctx legitimately differs); a *raw* dictionary is a no-op for `blockIndependent` frames (the per-block one-shot reset discards it); and `LZ4F_compressBound` always budgets a full block.\n\n**One agent's exclusion reasons were factually wrong** and I corrected them: it claimed lz4hc's asserts were live. `nm -u` per object file shows assert liveness differs by translation unit — compiled *out* in lz4.c/lz4hc.c/lz4frame.c (their own `LZ4_DEBUG`-gated no-op macro), *live* in lz4file.c/xxhash.c. This matters: it turns some lz4frame rows into testable ones and changes the correct reason for others. Two ERRORS.md rows also had inaccuracies I verified and fixed.\n\nSince \"zero divergences\" in the other modules is a suspicious result, those suites were mutation-tested and carry permanent `#[should_panic]` self-checks plus an assertion that the two libraries load at distinct addresses — one surviving mutation exposed a real gap in the xxhash `copyState` test, which was then strengthened."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":414070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":609,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bf83431-1376-4c81-bcb4-7fd267eb113b","uuid":"ae859dd8-d9b5-4b45-b2bb-04dad2d5e3a1","timestamp":"2026-08-23T10:08:53.112Z"}
